1
00:00:18,396 --> 00:00:21,605
[mysterious music playing]

2
00:00:44,938 --> 00:00:46,063
[man] Neil!

3
00:00:47,188 --> 00:00:48,480
[woman] Neil!

4
00:00:49,063 --> 00:00:52,187
[dogs barking]

5
00:00:52,188 --> 00:00:53,480
[man] Neil Spencer!

6
00:00:53,980 --> 00:00:55,688
[woman] Neil Spencer!

7
00:00:57,938 --> 00:00:59,105
[man] Neil!

8
00:00:59,938 --> 00:01:02,104
Anything more on the parents?

9
00:01:02,105 --> 00:01:04,229
[man 2] <i>Background checks
dug up nothing new.</i>

10
00:01:04,230 --> 00:01:08,480
<i>Dad's AWOL, mom's in rehab,
grandma's been taking care of the boy.</i>

11
00:01:09,105 --> 00:01:09,938
All right.

12
00:01:10,438 --> 00:01:12,645
I want all interviews
with immediate family in the area

13
00:01:12,646 --> 00:01:13,937
complete by the end of the day.

14
00:01:13,938 --> 00:01:15,188
[man 2] <i>Yes, Detective.</i>

15
00:01:16,438 --> 00:01:17,396
[man 1] Neil!

16
00:01:18,021 --> 00:01:20,187
- Neil!
- [woman over radio] <i>This is not a race.</i>

17
00:01:20,188 --> 00:01:22,520
<i>Take your time.
We're looking for a missing child.</i>

18
00:01:22,521 --> 00:01:24,105
All right, people.

19
00:01:24,646 --> 00:01:25,645
Listen up!

20
00:01:25,646 --> 00:01:28,895
All right, Neil Spencer was put to bed
around 8:00 p.m. last night.

21
00:01:28,896 --> 00:01:32,979
His grandmother reported him missing
at 10:29 p.m.

22
00:01:32,980 --> 00:01:36,145
Be prepared to call your families
and let them know you won't be home.

23
00:01:36,146 --> 00:01:38,770
[man 3] Detective! We found something.

24
00:01:38,771 --> 00:01:40,938
[tense music playing]

25
00:01:49,605 --> 00:01:51,605
[somber piano music playing]

26
00:02:08,938 --> 00:02:10,730
This isn't Neil Spencer.

27
00:02:28,105 --> 00:02:29,187
[music fades]

28
00:02:29,188 --> 00:02:32,188
["Shiny Happy People" by R.E.M.
playing over radio]

29
00:02:33,605 --> 00:02:36,854
<i>♪ Meet me in the crowd… ♪</i>

30
00:02:36,855 --> 00:02:39,688
You know, I'm excited.
It's a fresh start, right?

31
00:02:41,730 --> 00:02:42,812
- Yeah?
- Yeah.

32
00:02:42,813 --> 00:02:46,271
You know, your mom always wanted us
to move back to the town we grew up in.

33
00:02:46,771 --> 00:02:49,979
You know, it's cool. You'll be going
to the same school she did. Right?

34
00:02:49,980 --> 00:02:51,188
- Yeah.
- [dad] Yeah.

35
00:02:52,188 --> 00:02:54,395
Plus, we found a house with a swing.

36
00:02:54,396 --> 00:02:57,729
I mean, it's just like the one
you guys loved at the shore.

37
00:02:57,730 --> 00:02:59,562
You've said.

38
00:02:59,563 --> 00:03:01,145
Like a thousand times.

39
00:03:01,146 --> 00:03:02,812
No, no, no. No, that's incorrect.

40
00:03:02,813 --> 00:03:04,979
I've only said it 936 times.

41
00:03:04,980 --> 00:03:06,938
- [chuckles]
- [dad] So get your facts straight.

42
00:03:11,813 --> 00:03:13,105
I miss her.

43
00:03:16,021 --> 00:03:17,188
Me too, buddy.

44
00:03:19,896 --> 00:03:23,021
Up! Get your legs up.
Get 'em up. Come on. Up, up, up, up, up!

45
00:03:24,313 --> 00:03:27,520
And… we are in Garretton.

46
00:03:27,521 --> 00:03:29,312
<i>♪ Everyone around… ♪</i>

47
00:03:29,313 --> 00:03:30,271
We did it.

48
00:03:30,980 --> 00:03:34,979
<i>♪ Love them, love them ♪</i>

49
00:03:34,980 --> 00:03:38,562
<i>♪ Put it in your hands ♪</i>

50
00:03:38,563 --> 00:03:42,313
<i>♪ Take it, take it… ♪</i>

51
00:03:44,271 --> 00:03:45,354
[radio turns off]

52
00:03:45,355 --> 00:03:47,355
[indistinct chatter in background]

53
00:03:59,313 --> 00:04:00,438
There it is.

54
00:04:01,938 --> 00:04:03,312
- Wanna go check it out?
- Yeah.

55
00:04:03,313 --> 00:04:04,188
Go ahead.

56
00:04:05,730 --> 00:04:07,062
- Hey, guys.
- [man 1] What's up?

57
00:04:07,063 --> 00:04:10,229
[man 2] Hey, how you doing?
Uh, where do you want these, sir?

58
00:04:10,230 --> 00:04:13,271
[dad] Yeah, you know what?
Those can go in the kitchen. Thank you.

59
00:04:19,521 --> 00:04:22,480
- [kid] Hey, Dad! Look at this!
- Be right there, buddy.

60
00:04:32,188 --> 00:04:34,688
I hope this place is
big enough for you, Jake.

61
00:04:36,605 --> 00:04:38,605
[mysterious music playing]

62
00:04:48,646 --> 00:04:51,812
All right, come on, kiddo.
We got a new house, new stairs.

63
00:04:51,813 --> 00:04:53,355
What did we say we were gonna be?

64
00:04:55,813 --> 00:04:56,938
[whispers] Brave.

65
00:04:57,438 --> 00:04:58,563
That's right.

66
00:04:59,188 --> 00:05:01,480
Just like your mom when she was sick.

67
00:05:03,646 --> 00:05:04,480
Come here.

68
00:05:06,230 --> 00:05:09,438
All right. Let's go upstairs.

69
00:05:10,063 --> 00:05:11,188
Yeah.

70
00:05:15,271 --> 00:05:17,230
And…

71
00:05:18,063 --> 00:05:19,188
Go find your room.

72
00:05:49,730 --> 00:05:50,938
What's wrong?

73
00:05:52,355 --> 00:05:54,105
Why are you so scared?

74
00:05:57,271 --> 00:05:58,563
It's gonna be fine.

75
00:06:02,688 --> 00:06:05,270
[dad] No, not… No! Wait a second.

76
00:06:05,271 --> 00:06:06,479
You can't take him.

77
00:06:06,480 --> 00:06:08,104
Okay, Saturn's going…

78
00:06:08,105 --> 00:06:10,229
Do-do-do-do-do-do!

79
00:06:10,230 --> 00:06:11,229
…right up to the sun.

80
00:06:11,230 --> 00:06:12,229
Do-do-do-do!

81
00:06:12,230 --> 00:06:13,812
- [Jake] No!
- [dad] Chain reaction.

82
00:06:13,813 --> 00:06:14,729
No!

83
00:06:14,730 --> 00:06:16,520
Oh no!

84
00:06:16,521 --> 00:06:18,521
[excited chatter in background]

85
00:06:19,730 --> 00:06:21,187
All right. Uh…

86
00:06:21,188 --> 00:06:22,854
- Okay. You ready?
- [Jake] Yeah.

87
00:06:22,855 --> 00:06:24,855
Good? It's gonna be great. Okay?

88
00:06:26,146 --> 00:06:29,271
You warm enough?
Yeah? Wanna hang onto that?

89
00:06:30,021 --> 00:06:30,855
You sure?

90
00:06:31,813 --> 00:06:33,020
Yeah?

91
00:06:33,021 --> 00:06:34,145
Okay. All right.

92
00:06:34,146 --> 00:06:35,188
Come here.

93
00:06:36,230 --> 00:06:38,395
All right. Have a good day, okay?

94
00:06:38,396 --> 00:06:40,730
I'm gonna be right here
when school gets out, all right?

95
00:06:41,230 --> 00:06:43,480
- Okay. Okay?
- Hmm.

96
00:06:53,896 --> 00:06:58,730
[thunder rumbling]

97
00:07:23,605 --> 00:07:27,313
[slow tapping]

98
00:07:32,105 --> 00:07:34,271
Oh fuck.

99
00:07:41,271 --> 00:07:42,605
Jesus.

100
00:07:47,438 --> 00:07:50,646
[rain dripping slowly]

101
00:07:56,563 --> 00:07:58,771
[tapping on keyboard]

102
00:08:12,438 --> 00:08:14,521
[unsettling music playing]

103
00:08:18,646 --> 00:08:21,188
<i>If your window's left unlatched</i>

104
00:08:22,021 --> 00:08:24,562
<i>You'll hear him tapping at the glass</i>

105
00:08:24,563 --> 00:08:27,980
[kettle whistling]

106
00:08:38,355 --> 00:08:42,188
[unsettling music building]

107
00:09:51,896 --> 00:09:53,896
[somber music playing]

108
00:09:54,688 --> 00:09:56,688
[man whispering on tape]
<i>What kind of fish were they?</i>

109
00:09:57,188 --> 00:09:58,729
[Tony] <i>I don't know.</i>

110
00:09:58,730 --> 00:10:02,146
<i>There was a pink one. And a blue one.</i>

111
00:10:03,063 --> 00:10:05,021
[Whisper Man] <i>Do you think
they'll miss you?</i>

112
00:10:05,813 --> 00:10:07,395
[Tony] <i>My fish?</i>

113
00:10:07,396 --> 00:10:10,646
[Whisper Man] <i>You fed them, right?
Like your daddy fed you.</i>

114
00:10:11,146 --> 00:10:14,396
<i>Do you think they'll miss you
feeding them?</i>

115
00:10:15,730 --> 00:10:18,313
- [Tony mumbles] <i>I don't know.</i>
- [Whisper Man] <i>Speak up, boy.</i>

116
00:10:18,896 --> 00:10:21,146
<i>What if they get hungry
and you're not there?</i>

117
00:10:21,646 --> 00:10:23,605
<i>Do you think they'll eat each other?</i>

118
00:10:24,355 --> 00:10:28,729
<i>When one fish is shitting out the other,
will they be thinking of you?</i>

119
00:10:28,730 --> 00:10:31,355
[unsettling music]

120
00:10:37,563 --> 00:10:38,730
[man] Good.

121
00:10:40,021 --> 00:10:42,521
Good. I think they're going to love this.

122
00:10:47,146 --> 00:10:48,563
That's for later.

123
00:11:21,271 --> 00:11:22,895
[banging on door]

124
00:11:22,896 --> 00:11:25,896
[thunder rumbling, rain pattering]

125
00:11:29,896 --> 00:11:31,271
[woman] Hi, Mr. Willis.

126
00:11:31,771 --> 00:11:34,146
Uh, Detective Amanda Beck, Garretton PD.

127
00:11:34,646 --> 00:11:35,605
May I come in?

128
00:11:36,771 --> 00:11:38,521
I'm sorry to interrupt your dinner.

129
00:11:39,146 --> 00:11:42,395
Uh, a boy went missing
in Hillcrest a couple of days ago.

130
00:11:42,396 --> 00:11:43,729
Neil Spencer.

131
00:11:43,730 --> 00:11:46,271
We've cleared locations,
family, and friends.

132
00:11:46,896 --> 00:11:50,646
We found something, and I don't know
if it's a lead or a distraction.

133
00:11:54,688 --> 00:11:56,645
Another body. A boy.

134
00:11:56,646 --> 00:11:58,563
Been out in the woods about a month.

135
00:12:04,771 --> 00:12:06,895
Not every kid
who disappears in North Jersey

136
00:12:06,896 --> 00:12:08,895
is connected to Frank Carter, Detective.

137
00:12:08,896 --> 00:12:10,854
But that's his signature, right?

138
00:12:10,855 --> 00:12:13,396
Well, Frank Carter's doing life
in Rahway now.

139
00:12:14,313 --> 00:12:15,438
That's not what I asked.

140
00:12:17,146 --> 00:12:21,020
I know you need to find him, of course,
but I don't know if I can help you.

141
00:12:21,021 --> 00:12:23,145
[Beck] The other boy who went missing,
Neil Spencer,

142
00:12:23,146 --> 00:12:26,938
told his grandma he heard a strange voice
outside his window

143
00:12:27,771 --> 00:12:29,063
whispering to him.

144
00:12:31,730 --> 00:12:34,479
Well, you know,
kids have active imaginations--

145
00:12:34,480 --> 00:12:37,145
Yes, that's what Carter preyed on.
That's what you said.

146
00:12:37,146 --> 00:12:39,312
I did, but, you know,
I'm not on the job anymore.

147
00:12:39,313 --> 00:12:42,187
It's been a long time.
I'm retired at least 25 years.

148
00:12:42,188 --> 00:12:44,479
I just, you know…
And there's only one Frank Carter.

149
00:12:44,480 --> 00:12:48,937
Your case file mentioned an accomplice
to Carter who was never identified.

150
00:12:48,938 --> 00:12:51,520
I did. I did.
It was a theory, and it went cold.

151
00:12:51,521 --> 00:12:52,521
They often do.

152
00:12:59,896 --> 00:13:03,062
Frank Carter still declines all interviews
via his lawyers.

153
00:13:03,063 --> 00:13:05,604
You remain the only one
he's ever agreed to speak with

154
00:13:05,605 --> 00:13:08,563
since his, uh, incarceration.

155
00:13:09,688 --> 00:13:11,562
Got any advice interviewing him?

156
00:13:11,563 --> 00:13:13,355
Yeah, I'd say don't.

157
00:13:16,146 --> 00:13:18,105
I… I hope you find your kid.

158
00:13:18,605 --> 00:13:21,480
With all due respect, sir,
hope does nothing for me.

159
00:13:27,980 --> 00:13:29,980
[unsettling music playing]

160
00:13:57,771 --> 00:14:00,812
Can I put this
in my Packet of Special Things?

161
00:14:00,813 --> 00:14:02,230
Let me see.

162
00:14:07,730 --> 00:14:08,563
Sure.

163
00:14:15,438 --> 00:14:16,646
What's that?

164
00:14:17,313 --> 00:14:19,979
We made our hands be in paint
on the wall at school.

165
00:14:19,980 --> 00:14:21,770
Oh, yeah? Handprints, huh?

166
00:14:21,771 --> 00:14:23,229
- [Jake] Mm-hmm.
- Cool.

167
00:14:23,230 --> 00:14:24,605
My friend helped me.

168
00:14:26,396 --> 00:14:28,438
Oh, yeah? You make a friend?

169
00:14:29,438 --> 00:14:31,146
The girl in the blue sweater.

170
00:14:33,355 --> 00:14:36,145
Well, do you remember
we talked about that?

171
00:14:36,146 --> 00:14:38,521
How some friends are pretend and…

172
00:14:42,563 --> 00:14:43,730
What's up, bud?

173
00:14:46,105 --> 00:14:48,145
Are you sure she won't wake up?

174
00:14:48,146 --> 00:14:49,105
[Tom] Mommy?

175
00:14:50,521 --> 00:14:51,646
I am.

176
00:14:54,063 --> 00:14:56,396
You know, Mommy loved you

177
00:14:57,563 --> 00:15:01,730
more than anything, you know,
and that's… that's never gonna change.

178
00:15:02,271 --> 00:15:06,437
But it doesn't mean
that you can't make room for new people,

179
00:15:06,438 --> 00:15:08,730
you know, new… new friends.

180
00:15:09,396 --> 00:15:11,938
I don't like the boys at school.

181
00:15:15,188 --> 00:15:16,105
You know,

182
00:15:17,021 --> 00:15:18,562
I never told you this,

183
00:15:18,563 --> 00:15:23,604
but when I was your age,
I had a friend, just like you have.

184
00:15:23,605 --> 00:15:24,604
I did.

185
00:15:24,605 --> 00:15:27,771
He'd visit me when I was going to sleep,
and we'd go on adventures.

186
00:15:28,438 --> 00:15:30,062
At the end, every time,

187
00:15:30,063 --> 00:15:32,562
he would kiss me on the forehead,
right here.

188
00:15:32,563 --> 00:15:33,646
And then

189
00:15:34,521 --> 00:15:38,480
I'd wake up the next morning
back in bed like magic.

190
00:15:39,105 --> 00:15:41,480
I called him Mr. Night. [chuckles]

191
00:15:42,271 --> 00:15:43,437
[chuckles]

192
00:15:43,438 --> 00:15:46,395
It's okay to imagine things, Jake.

193
00:15:46,396 --> 00:15:48,146
You just… You gotta

194
00:15:49,063 --> 00:15:51,688
give real people a chance, too, okay?

195
00:16:05,063 --> 00:16:07,438
[high-pitched eerie music playing]

196
00:16:18,063 --> 00:16:19,646
[softly] What is your name?

197
00:16:25,938 --> 00:16:27,188
[man whispers] It's okay.

198
00:16:28,313 --> 00:16:30,021
They need to hear this.

199
00:16:32,230 --> 00:16:35,063
[low thrumming]

200
00:16:37,771 --> 00:16:39,771
[eerie music building]

201
00:16:48,396 --> 00:16:50,605
[tense music playing]

202
00:17:01,521 --> 00:17:03,521
[indistinct background chatter]

203
00:17:22,355 --> 00:17:24,437
[music fades]

204
00:17:24,438 --> 00:17:26,812
[excited background chatter]

205
00:17:26,813 --> 00:17:29,479
[Tom] Hey! Sorry! Sorry, I'm late.

206
00:17:29,480 --> 00:17:32,438
- You're Jake's father?
- Yeah, yeah, yeah. Hi. How you doing?

207
00:17:33,230 --> 00:17:34,687
Buddy, what's wrong?

208
00:17:34,688 --> 00:17:36,855
[woman] You wanna tell your dad
what happened?

209
00:17:37,646 --> 00:17:39,437
I got put on yellow.

210
00:17:39,438 --> 00:17:40,812
You… On what?

211
00:17:40,813 --> 00:17:43,313
We have a traffic light system
for bad behavior.

212
00:17:43,896 --> 00:17:46,021
What'd he do? Uh, what'd you do?

213
00:17:46,605 --> 00:17:49,312
Owen tried to take
my Packet of Special Things.

214
00:17:49,313 --> 00:17:51,770
He scratched a boy. Badly.

215
00:17:51,771 --> 00:17:55,062
Okay, well, that's…
You can't do that, Jake.

216
00:17:55,063 --> 00:17:57,604
Um, sorry. It's this packet.

217
00:17:57,605 --> 00:18:01,312
Um, it's full of stuff that,
like, belonged to his mom.

218
00:18:01,313 --> 00:18:02,771
That's no excuse.

219
00:18:03,605 --> 00:18:06,605
We'd like him to write a note apologizing.

220
00:18:07,938 --> 00:18:09,854
Uh, isn't that excessive?

221
00:18:09,855 --> 00:18:12,437
We have zero tolerance
for kids hurting kids.

222
00:18:12,438 --> 00:18:14,062
What's your tolerance for bullies?

223
00:18:14,063 --> 00:18:16,604
'Cause that other kid
sounds like kind of a dick.

224
00:18:16,605 --> 00:18:19,604
- [woman] Excuse me?
- You know what? We'll pass on that note.

225
00:18:19,605 --> 00:18:20,521
Come on, buddy.

226
00:18:21,688 --> 00:18:23,271
You can put me on yellow.

227
00:18:29,813 --> 00:18:30,771
[Beck] Where is it?

228
00:18:35,771 --> 00:18:38,937
[Neil] <i>I didn't like being there,</i>

229
00:18:38,938 --> 00:18:40,563
<i>that house.</i>

230
00:18:41,105 --> 00:18:42,813
[man whispering] <i>Your grandmother's.</i>

231
00:18:43,688 --> 00:18:45,813
<i>Was she mean to you</i>?

232
00:18:46,855 --> 00:18:49,313
[Neil] <i>No. Sometimes</i>

233
00:18:49,938 --> 00:18:51,563
<i>she was sick.</i>

234
00:18:52,980 --> 00:18:54,480
<i>I was afraid.</i>

235
00:18:55,105 --> 00:18:56,521
[man] <i>It's okay.</i>

236
00:18:57,313 --> 00:18:59,146
<i>They need to hear it.</i>

237
00:19:00,855 --> 00:19:03,270
[Neil] <i>I was afraid she'd die.</i>

238
00:19:03,271 --> 00:19:07,063
<i>She'd be dead in the house with me
while I slept.</i>

239
00:19:08,313 --> 00:19:11,438
[man] <i>If you could talk to your mommy
right now,</i>

240
00:19:12,355 --> 00:19:13,771
<i>what would you say?</i>

241
00:19:16,063 --> 00:19:18,188
[Neil] <i>Why did you leave me there?</i>

242
00:19:18,896 --> 00:19:20,688
<i>Why don't you love me?</i>

243
00:19:22,313 --> 00:19:23,730
[man] <i>I love you.</i>

244
00:19:26,355 --> 00:19:30,355
[on tape] <i>♪ Free your mind
And the rest will follow ♪</i>

245
00:19:30,896 --> 00:19:33,354
<i>♪ Be color blind ♪</i>

246
00:19:33,355 --> 00:19:35,021
<i>♪ Don't be so shallow ♪</i>

247
00:19:35,980 --> 00:19:40,021
<i>♪ Free your mind
And the rest will follow ♪</i>

248
00:19:40,521 --> 00:19:41,521
[song ends]

249
00:19:50,688 --> 00:19:53,688
[wind howling]

250
00:19:56,230 --> 00:19:57,230
[soft thud]

251
00:19:58,105 --> 00:20:00,188
[tapping]

252
00:20:06,813 --> 00:20:09,895
[tapping]

253
00:20:09,896 --> 00:20:11,896
[wind continues howling]

254
00:20:15,688 --> 00:20:16,688
[soft thud]

255
00:20:22,521 --> 00:20:23,521
[thud]

256
00:20:41,438 --> 00:20:43,063
[ominous music]

257
00:20:51,271 --> 00:20:54,229
[Jake quietly]
<i>If you leave a door half open</i>

258
00:20:54,230 --> 00:20:56,855
<i>Soon you'll hear the whispers spoken</i>

259
00:20:57,563 --> 00:20:59,812
<i>If your window is left unlatched</i>

260
00:20:59,813 --> 00:21:02,271
<i>You'll hear him tapping at the glass</i>

261
00:21:03,313 --> 00:21:04,355
Jake?

262
00:21:05,730 --> 00:21:06,938
What are you doing?

263
00:21:08,188 --> 00:21:10,188
[sinister music]

264
00:21:11,688 --> 00:21:12,605
Jake!

265
00:21:13,605 --> 00:21:14,730
No!

266
00:21:18,313 --> 00:21:20,313
[dramatic music playing]

267
00:21:27,730 --> 00:21:29,104
Who were you talking to?

268
00:21:29,105 --> 00:21:30,438
Nobody.

269
00:21:34,146 --> 00:21:36,312
[wind howling]

270
00:21:36,313 --> 00:21:40,645
[slow tapping]

271
00:21:40,646 --> 00:21:42,396
[rattling]

272
00:21:45,396 --> 00:21:46,313
Back to bed.

273
00:21:47,813 --> 00:21:49,813
[tapping and creaking]

274
00:21:57,896 --> 00:22:01,730
[wind continues howling]

275
00:22:04,563 --> 00:22:07,563
[soft mysterious piano music playing]

276
00:22:20,855 --> 00:22:21,896
[thud]

277
00:22:25,605 --> 00:22:26,730
[sighs]

278
00:22:46,813 --> 00:22:47,855
[Tom] Hey!

279
00:22:50,896 --> 00:22:53,270
Hey! What are you doing?

280
00:22:53,271 --> 00:22:55,687
Hey! Hey! Hey!

281
00:22:55,688 --> 00:22:56,813
[grunts]

282
00:22:57,646 --> 00:22:59,646
[groans]

283
00:23:02,063 --> 00:23:05,979
[man] We've had reports of a squatter
since the place went vacant.

284
00:23:05,980 --> 00:23:10,145
Kids sneaking in to drink
and do other things.

285
00:23:10,146 --> 00:23:11,730
This wasn't a kid.

286
00:23:14,230 --> 00:23:15,105
What's back here?

287
00:23:16,688 --> 00:23:17,813
I don't know.

288
00:23:24,230 --> 00:23:26,146
- Holy shit.
- [officer] Ooh.

289
00:23:30,855 --> 00:23:32,188
- Whoa.
- Previous owner?

290
00:23:32,688 --> 00:23:33,646
Um…

291
00:23:35,271 --> 00:23:36,438
[Tom] So now what?

292
00:23:37,688 --> 00:23:39,395
Well, he didn't attack you.

293
00:23:39,396 --> 00:23:42,479
He just bolted for the door
unless there's something else.

294
00:23:42,480 --> 00:23:44,855
He's most likely just a squatter.

295
00:23:45,480 --> 00:23:47,020
Left something here.

296
00:23:47,021 --> 00:23:49,312
Didn't realize the place was rented.

297
00:23:49,313 --> 00:23:51,354
Change the locks,
set up a security system,

298
00:23:51,355 --> 00:23:53,438
and donate this stuff to the Goodwill.

299
00:23:53,938 --> 00:23:55,980
And don't forget to bolt your back door.

300
00:23:58,313 --> 00:23:59,396
So that's it?

301
00:23:59,896 --> 00:24:02,771
[officer] Fresh coat of paint
on the outside might help ward people off.

302
00:24:13,855 --> 00:24:15,855
[wind howling]

303
00:24:53,688 --> 00:24:56,437
[Jake] <i>If you're lonely, sad, and blue</i>

304
00:24:56,438 --> 00:24:58,854
<i>The Whisper Man will come for you</i>

305
00:24:58,855 --> 00:25:00,771
[soft pulsing music playing]

306
00:25:02,355 --> 00:25:05,062
[Jake talking softly on video]

307
00:25:05,063 --> 00:25:07,187
[Jake quietly] <i>If your window's
left unlatched</i>

308
00:25:07,188 --> 00:25:09,104
<i>You'll hear him tapping at the…</i>

309
00:25:09,105 --> 00:25:10,770
Jake, what are you doing?

310
00:25:10,771 --> 00:25:11,980
Nothing.

311
00:25:12,563 --> 00:25:13,687
[Tom sighs]

312
00:25:13,688 --> 00:25:16,813
[wind howling]

313
00:25:17,563 --> 00:25:18,521
[Tom] Okay.

314
00:25:19,230 --> 00:25:20,605
Who are you talking to?

315
00:25:22,855 --> 00:25:24,438
Is it the girl in the blue sweater?

316
00:25:27,896 --> 00:25:30,895
She's scared of it here.

317
00:25:30,896 --> 00:25:33,313
She's scared of it here?
She's scared of this house? Why?

318
00:25:34,313 --> 00:25:36,355
She's scared of the boy who lives here.

319
00:25:37,521 --> 00:25:38,438
You?

320
00:25:40,230 --> 00:25:41,187
Who?

321
00:25:41,188 --> 00:25:45,145
The boy in the floor. Good God.

322
00:25:45,146 --> 00:25:47,520
Jake, you have to stop this.

323
00:25:47,521 --> 00:25:48,687
Stop what?

324
00:25:48,688 --> 00:25:51,105
Well… Ow! Goddammit!

325
00:25:52,646 --> 00:25:55,562
Pretending. I need you to grow up.

326
00:25:55,563 --> 00:25:57,229
You never believe me.

327
00:25:57,230 --> 00:25:58,437
[Tom] I can see you.

328
00:25:58,438 --> 00:26:00,020
I can see everything,

329
00:26:00,021 --> 00:26:03,229
and I know there is no one in here, Jake.

330
00:26:03,230 --> 00:26:05,855
You are just talking to yourself.

331
00:26:09,605 --> 00:26:10,480
[sighs]

332
00:26:22,855 --> 00:26:25,855
[high-pitched eerie music playing]

333
00:26:27,230 --> 00:26:28,230
[silence]

334
00:26:46,646 --> 00:26:48,646
[soft pulsing music playing]

335
00:26:51,313 --> 00:26:52,271
[Tom] Jake?

336
00:26:56,980 --> 00:26:57,896
Wha…

337
00:27:00,355 --> 00:27:02,355
[tense music playing]

338
00:27:05,980 --> 00:27:07,063
Jake?

339
00:27:09,980 --> 00:27:11,270
[yelling] Jake!

340
00:27:11,271 --> 00:27:12,146
Jake!

341
00:27:13,313 --> 00:27:14,271
Jake!

342
00:27:15,313 --> 00:27:16,271
Jake!

343
00:27:20,605 --> 00:27:22,021
Jake!

344
00:27:25,480 --> 00:27:26,396
Jake!

345
00:27:27,980 --> 00:27:30,063
Jake!

346
00:27:31,146 --> 00:27:32,313
Jake!

347
00:27:33,480 --> 00:27:34,521
Jake!

348
00:27:38,188 --> 00:27:40,188
[sirens wailing]

349
00:27:59,438 --> 00:28:02,480
I'm Detective Beck.
Tell me a little bit about Jake.

350
00:28:04,563 --> 00:28:05,521
Okay.

351
00:28:07,605 --> 00:28:08,521
[Beck] I know.

352
00:28:09,730 --> 00:28:11,562
- It's terrifying.
- [Tom moans softly]

353
00:28:11,563 --> 00:28:13,770
[breathes unsteadily]

354
00:28:13,771 --> 00:28:14,855
He's quiet.

355
00:28:15,355 --> 00:28:16,355
[Beck] It's hard.

356
00:28:17,480 --> 00:28:20,813
But we don't know which detail
is gonna help us find him.

357
00:28:24,271 --> 00:28:25,230
Okay.

358
00:28:28,646 --> 00:28:29,771
He, uh…

359
00:28:30,563 --> 00:28:33,230
He's a collector, you know, of…

360
00:28:34,896 --> 00:28:38,187
just, like, scraps of… of odds and ends.

361
00:28:38,188 --> 00:28:39,521
You know, like, um,

362
00:28:40,730 --> 00:28:45,062
ticket stubs and… and… and ribbon
and rocks even.

363
00:28:45,063 --> 00:28:47,437
It… it all has meaning to him.

364
00:28:47,438 --> 00:28:49,771
- That's nice.
- Yeah, he's a nice kid.

365
00:28:50,355 --> 00:28:51,438
What about his friends?

366
00:28:52,730 --> 00:28:53,729
[over radio] <i>Stand by.</i>

367
00:28:53,730 --> 00:28:57,980
We just moved, and, uh, you know,
school is just getting started, so…

368
00:28:58,646 --> 00:28:59,605
From where?

369
00:29:01,021 --> 00:29:04,230
- The Shore. Uh, Manasquan.
- [Beck] Hmm.

370
00:29:04,730 --> 00:29:06,687
Jake's mom grew up here, so…

371
00:29:06,688 --> 00:29:08,730
She's… gone.

372
00:29:09,688 --> 00:29:11,687
She was sick.

373
00:29:11,688 --> 00:29:13,688
[indistinct chatter over radio]

374
00:29:14,813 --> 00:29:16,771
Any other family nearby?

375
00:29:18,855 --> 00:29:19,979
My father.

376
00:29:19,980 --> 00:29:22,270
He's, uh… somewhere.

377
00:29:22,271 --> 00:29:24,021
I don't know. He's never met Jake.

378
00:29:25,855 --> 00:29:27,188
What's his name?

379
00:29:28,480 --> 00:29:31,396
Peter Willis. He was a cop.

380
00:29:37,105 --> 00:29:39,146
And have you called him? Your father?

381
00:29:40,146 --> 00:29:41,105
No.

382
00:29:43,355 --> 00:29:45,105
We looked at the nanny cam,

383
00:29:46,271 --> 00:29:50,105
and he left on his own.
There was no one else.

384
00:29:50,646 --> 00:29:52,437
[Tom breathes shakily]

385
00:29:52,438 --> 00:29:54,438
[unsettling music playing]

386
00:29:57,355 --> 00:29:58,396
Detective.

387
00:30:03,605 --> 00:30:04,521
What the fuck?

388
00:30:05,771 --> 00:30:06,688
Jesus.

389
00:30:07,188 --> 00:30:09,188
[unsettling music building]

390
00:30:19,271 --> 00:30:21,396
[indistinct chatter over radio]

391
00:30:28,563 --> 00:30:29,563
[sniffs]

392
00:30:42,396 --> 00:30:44,938
[unsettling music continues]

393
00:30:54,480 --> 00:30:56,896
[phone ringing]

394
00:31:05,063 --> 00:31:06,145
[music fades]

395
00:31:06,146 --> 00:31:07,063
Hello?

396
00:31:08,021 --> 00:31:08,980
[Tom] <i>Dad?</i>

397
00:31:11,730 --> 00:31:13,480
[door opens, bell jingles]

398
00:31:40,146 --> 00:31:43,230
[footsteps approaching]

399
00:31:45,980 --> 00:31:47,105
[server] What can I get you?

400
00:31:48,021 --> 00:31:50,021
Uh, I'll just have a coffee, yeah.

401
00:31:50,646 --> 00:31:52,105
You want coffee?

402
00:31:53,230 --> 00:31:54,813
- [server] Two coffees?
- [Pete] Yeah.

403
00:32:04,896 --> 00:32:06,188
How you holding up?

404
00:32:11,480 --> 00:32:14,438
I just need to know
they're doing everything they can. Okay?

405
00:32:15,021 --> 00:32:16,563
I'm doing everything I can.

406
00:32:17,563 --> 00:32:18,438
Sure.

407
00:32:19,980 --> 00:32:22,062
At the department,
you still have friends there.

408
00:32:22,063 --> 00:32:23,605
I mean, you still have pull.

409
00:32:24,855 --> 00:32:28,063
I was young. I… I don't remember much.

410
00:32:28,813 --> 00:32:32,687
But I remember the Whisper Man,
and I remember you found him.

411
00:32:32,688 --> 00:32:34,187
I found him. I did do that.

412
00:32:34,188 --> 00:32:35,270
[server approaching]

413
00:32:35,271 --> 00:32:36,188
[Tom] So…

414
00:32:44,813 --> 00:32:45,979
He's a good kid, Jake.

415
00:32:45,980 --> 00:32:47,688
He's smart, and…

416
00:32:49,438 --> 00:32:50,980
They got any leads?

417
00:32:51,480 --> 00:32:53,729
Well, yeah, I mean,
if they'd fucking follow 'em.

418
00:32:53,730 --> 00:32:55,063
That's why I need you.

419
00:32:55,563 --> 00:32:58,021
Well, I'm sure they've got
a good detective working the case.

420
00:32:58,605 --> 00:33:00,729
No, <i>you</i> were a good detective.

421
00:33:00,730 --> 00:33:04,145
You're a shitty father,
but a good fucking detective.

422
00:33:04,146 --> 00:33:05,479
They will listen to you,

423
00:33:05,480 --> 00:33:08,104
and they will tell you things
they won't tell me.

424
00:33:08,105 --> 00:33:09,312
I, um…

425
00:33:09,313 --> 00:33:10,480
Well, uh…

426
00:33:13,021 --> 00:33:15,188
Listen, I… I…

427
00:33:16,563 --> 00:33:20,645
I wanted to reach out earlier,
especially after Rebecca had passed away--

428
00:33:20,646 --> 00:33:21,605
Don't.

429
00:33:23,355 --> 00:33:24,271
Don't do that.

430
00:33:28,355 --> 00:33:32,187
- Sorry it took this to get us together.
- We're not. This isn't us together.

431
00:33:32,188 --> 00:33:34,521
This is me asking you for help.
Do you understand that?

432
00:33:39,146 --> 00:33:40,563
Sure, I understand that.

433
00:33:43,396 --> 00:33:46,730
I don't know what I can do, Tom. I…

434
00:33:49,521 --> 00:33:52,396
I haven't carried a shield in forever.

435
00:33:52,980 --> 00:33:54,646
I'm sure they don't wanna hear from me.

436
00:33:55,646 --> 00:33:57,270
But I am here for you, whatever--

437
00:33:57,271 --> 00:34:00,895
Excuse me. I don't need
your emotional fucking support, okay?

438
00:34:00,896 --> 00:34:03,771
I need you to find my boy!

439
00:34:13,896 --> 00:34:14,730
No? Great.

440
00:34:19,896 --> 00:34:21,313
[door opens]

441
00:34:31,938 --> 00:34:32,938
[sighs]

442
00:34:40,313 --> 00:34:43,313
[indistinct chatter, phones ringing]

443
00:34:47,396 --> 00:34:51,395
[Beck] Why'd Carter do that?
The T-shirt. Cover their faces.

444
00:34:51,396 --> 00:34:54,855
[Pete] Didn't want them looking at him.
He didn't wanna look at them.

445
00:35:06,313 --> 00:35:09,229
There's, uh, not much new here.
This is all you have?

446
00:35:09,230 --> 00:35:10,521
We're still playing catch-up.

447
00:35:12,021 --> 00:35:13,812
And Tom said he gave you a lead?

448
00:35:13,813 --> 00:35:16,312
Yeah. We have a loose description
of a vagrant he saw

449
00:35:16,313 --> 00:35:19,021
rummaging around his basement.
Haven't found a match yet.

450
00:35:21,980 --> 00:35:24,105
Uh, you should listen to the Spencer tape.

451
00:35:25,105 --> 00:35:27,729
[Pete] This is from the boy?
Blaming the parents.

452
00:35:27,730 --> 00:35:30,979
- Same as Frank Carter's Whisper Man.
- [Pete] Yeah, I've heard this.

453
00:35:30,980 --> 00:35:33,479
These kids aren't the only
intended victims.

454
00:35:33,480 --> 00:35:34,688
Forensics?

455
00:35:35,396 --> 00:35:38,729
The package was mishandled
at the TV station. It's tainted.

456
00:35:38,730 --> 00:35:42,021
Obviously, with the tape drop,
we know time is short.

457
00:35:44,980 --> 00:35:48,896
Tom said you never met him. Jake.

458
00:35:50,021 --> 00:35:50,980
May I ask why?

459
00:35:54,146 --> 00:35:58,313
Any connection between the two boys
other than they were found missing?

460
00:35:59,230 --> 00:36:01,020
Jake was new to town.

461
00:36:01,021 --> 00:36:03,479
Uh, different elementary
as the Spencer boy

462
00:36:03,480 --> 00:36:04,980
who went to Catholic school.

463
00:36:05,480 --> 00:36:08,063
Stevie Grant was in foster care.

464
00:36:09,355 --> 00:36:11,355
We're looking
at a few local sex offenders.

465
00:36:12,063 --> 00:36:15,520
You speculated in the Carter case
that the boys somehow

466
00:36:15,521 --> 00:36:17,479
walked out of their homes on their own.

467
00:36:17,480 --> 00:36:21,480
That Frank Carter… somehow summoned them.

468
00:36:22,480 --> 00:36:25,229
[Pete] Carter knew how to find
the ones who wanted to go.

469
00:36:25,230 --> 00:36:27,146
[unsettling music playing]

470
00:36:34,230 --> 00:36:35,396
[banging on door]

471
00:36:41,230 --> 00:36:42,188
From your house.

472
00:36:44,146 --> 00:36:46,646
What if my boy comes back home
and I'm not there?

473
00:36:47,146 --> 00:36:50,771
It's a crime scene.
Right now, this is best.

474
00:36:51,396 --> 00:36:53,313
Unless you have someone you can stay with.

475
00:37:13,813 --> 00:37:16,355
[tense music playing]

476
00:37:24,980 --> 00:37:26,313
[cell phone ringing]

477
00:37:26,980 --> 00:37:27,895
Beck here.

478
00:37:27,896 --> 00:37:31,854
The man who used to live in my house
did time at the East Jersey State Prison.

479
00:37:31,855 --> 00:37:32,688
[Beck] <i>Mr. Kennedy?</i>

480
00:37:33,313 --> 00:37:35,270
[Tom] <i>Yeah, I have his mail right here.</i>

481
00:37:35,271 --> 00:37:38,104
Dominic Barnett,
assaulting a police officer.

482
00:37:38,105 --> 00:37:40,937
- He got out fucking seven years ago.
- [Beck] <i>Slow down.</i>

483
00:37:40,938 --> 00:37:43,395
You're saying he lived at the house
that you're renting?

484
00:37:43,396 --> 00:37:45,437
It could be him.
Look, they were both at Rahway.

485
00:37:45,438 --> 00:37:47,520
And if he knew Carter
while they were inside--

486
00:37:47,521 --> 00:37:48,937
[Beck] <i>Uh, send me what you have,</i>

487
00:37:48,938 --> 00:37:51,396
okay, and I'll look into it.
Uh, Dominic Barnett, you say?

488
00:37:52,521 --> 00:37:54,729
This could be the guy.

489
00:37:54,730 --> 00:37:56,312
I said I'll look into it.

490
00:37:56,313 --> 00:37:57,729
<i>Okay? Thank you.</i>

491
00:37:57,730 --> 00:37:59,605
Are you… are you fucking kid…

492
00:38:00,688 --> 00:38:01,770
- [phone clatters]
- Fuck!

493
00:38:01,771 --> 00:38:03,270
Barnett, I know that name.

494
00:38:03,271 --> 00:38:07,312
He was a runner for the Brick Squad gang
back when I was on the job.

495
00:38:07,313 --> 00:38:10,020
[Beck] Yeah, they deal
out of the Wrigley Projects now.

496
00:38:10,021 --> 00:38:12,854
And how long between the time
when the kids were put to bed

497
00:38:12,855 --> 00:38:14,270
and when they disappeared?

498
00:38:14,271 --> 00:38:17,312
For the Spencer boy, not long.
Ninety minutes.

499
00:38:17,313 --> 00:38:18,396
Jake?

500
00:38:18,896 --> 00:38:21,355
Six hours before Tom woke up.

501
00:38:22,271 --> 00:38:24,604
He was drinking, maybe drunk.

502
00:38:24,605 --> 00:38:26,271
I could smell the alcohol.

503
00:38:28,396 --> 00:38:30,020
[Pete] I never met her.

504
00:38:30,021 --> 00:38:33,813
She called once,
wanted to tell me that she was pregnant.

505
00:38:35,230 --> 00:38:36,480
We talked for a bit.

506
00:38:38,146 --> 00:38:39,313
He was in good hands.

507
00:38:47,605 --> 00:38:48,980
Drawing wars.

508
00:38:49,480 --> 00:38:50,938
Tom did these too.

509
00:38:52,730 --> 00:38:54,896
You never know what gets passed on.

510
00:38:56,563 --> 00:38:58,563
[wind chimes tinkling]

511
00:38:59,688 --> 00:39:02,520
[dog barking]

512
00:39:02,521 --> 00:39:03,604
[woman] Hey!

513
00:39:03,605 --> 00:39:06,729
Mrs. Shearing.
I'm the guy renting your house.

514
00:39:06,730 --> 00:39:08,187
Tom. Tom Kennedy.

515
00:39:08,188 --> 00:39:10,229
You said you'd clear that shit out!

516
00:39:10,230 --> 00:39:11,479
- I'm not doing it for you!
- No!

517
00:39:11,480 --> 00:39:14,437
- Mrs. Shearing, please! My son is missing!
- Fuck off, Randall.

518
00:39:14,438 --> 00:39:15,521
[Tom] Please!

519
00:39:16,188 --> 00:39:18,021
[Beck] We should still interview him.

520
00:39:18,521 --> 00:39:21,729
Carter. He won't see anyone
unless you're there.

521
00:39:21,730 --> 00:39:26,395
[Pete] Yeah, all that bastard will do is
make you nauseous and want to throw up.

522
00:39:26,396 --> 00:39:27,979
When we zeroed in on him,

523
00:39:27,980 --> 00:39:30,687
Carter had managed
a day and a half on the run.

524
00:39:30,688 --> 00:39:32,395
And when we finally did get him,

525
00:39:32,396 --> 00:39:35,688
there was evidence that the fifth boy
he took, Tony Smith, was still alive.

526
00:39:36,188 --> 00:39:38,312
I did everything I could to find him.
Everything.

527
00:39:38,313 --> 00:39:41,187
I interrogated Carter's wife
at least six hours.

528
00:39:41,188 --> 00:39:42,979
And then I went to see Carter himself

529
00:39:42,980 --> 00:39:45,937
to appeal to what little bit of humanity
might be left in him.

530
00:39:45,938 --> 00:39:47,105
There was nothing.

531
00:39:48,480 --> 00:39:49,396
Nothing.

532
00:39:50,313 --> 00:39:53,312
Dominic Barnett. You rented to him?

533
00:39:53,313 --> 00:39:56,979
That nephew of mine ain't worth fuck all.

534
00:39:56,980 --> 00:39:58,437
Wait, you're related?

535
00:39:58,438 --> 00:40:01,770
Little shit up and cleared out
without paying six months' rent.

536
00:40:01,771 --> 00:40:05,480
Okay, is there anything you can tell me
about where to find him now?

537
00:40:07,855 --> 00:40:12,395
He had a girlfriend
at the Wrigley Park Projects.

538
00:40:12,396 --> 00:40:15,271
Okay, do you know her name,
the girlfriend?

539
00:40:17,188 --> 00:40:19,229
Tina… Tiffany.

540
00:40:19,230 --> 00:40:22,105
I do remember she lived… [laughs]

541
00:40:22,855 --> 00:40:24,895
…in Building C.

542
00:40:24,896 --> 00:40:26,313
For "cunt."

543
00:40:27,063 --> 00:40:29,063
[siren wailing in background]

544
00:40:36,605 --> 00:40:39,771
- [music playing over speakers]
- [indistinct chatter]

545
00:40:58,021 --> 00:40:59,730
[man shouting] Hey, yo, my peeps!

546
00:41:00,730 --> 00:41:01,730
Everybody out here!

547
00:41:13,438 --> 00:41:15,354
[indistinct voices in background]

548
00:41:15,355 --> 00:41:16,770
[door slams]

549
00:41:16,771 --> 00:41:17,895
[dog barking]

550
00:41:17,896 --> 00:41:19,896
[indistinct shouting]

551
00:41:21,855 --> 00:41:24,812
[man] How the fuck you don't hear me
when I'm fucking talking to you?!

552
00:41:24,813 --> 00:41:26,520
Look at me when I'm talking to you!

553
00:41:26,521 --> 00:41:30,396
[man continues shouting]

554
00:41:32,980 --> 00:41:34,895
[tense music playing]

555
00:41:34,896 --> 00:41:37,520
- Help you?
- Uh, no. No, thanks.

556
00:41:37,521 --> 00:41:39,021
What are you looking for?

557
00:41:40,021 --> 00:41:41,395
Dominic Barnett.

558
00:41:41,396 --> 00:41:43,145
Don't know no Barnett.

559
00:41:43,146 --> 00:41:44,521
- [woman] Nah.
- Okay.

560
00:41:49,313 --> 00:41:50,813
Are you buying, motherfucker?

561
00:41:51,563 --> 00:41:53,063
Apache, Murder 8.

562
00:41:53,563 --> 00:41:55,437
Ten for one. Three for twenty.

563
00:41:55,438 --> 00:41:56,812
Fentanyl, bitch.

564
00:41:56,813 --> 00:41:59,021
Oh, uh, no. No, thanks.

565
00:42:00,980 --> 00:42:02,895
[both grunt]

566
00:42:02,896 --> 00:42:06,104
Beat your motherfucking ass.
The fuck you think you doing? Huh?

567
00:42:06,105 --> 00:42:07,437
[man grunts]

568
00:42:07,438 --> 00:42:11,270
Both of you, get the fuck out of here.
I'll blow your head off, motherfucker.

569
00:42:11,271 --> 00:42:12,480
All right. Get up.

570
00:42:14,980 --> 00:42:17,480
[tense music continues]

571
00:42:19,813 --> 00:42:21,521
- What about my car--
- Get in. Get in.

572
00:42:23,688 --> 00:42:25,480
[man 2] Yo, get the fuck outta here.

573
00:42:31,438 --> 00:42:34,438
Give me the keys. I'll get somebody
to pick up the car. Just give me the keys.

574
00:42:37,646 --> 00:42:40,062
[Tom] Jesus fucking Christ.

575
00:42:40,063 --> 00:42:41,895
What the fuck? How are you here?

576
00:42:41,896 --> 00:42:45,395
You were right to wanna look at Barnett,
but you gotta trust these detectives.

577
00:42:45,396 --> 00:42:46,687
Let 'em do their job.

578
00:42:46,688 --> 00:42:48,770
And that Detective Beck?
She's not gonna let this go.

579
00:42:48,771 --> 00:42:50,145
- You talked to her?
- [Pete] Yes--

580
00:42:50,146 --> 00:42:52,730
- You talked to her?
- I was with her when you called.

581
00:42:54,230 --> 00:42:55,479
- You were?
- [Pete] I was.

582
00:42:55,480 --> 00:42:56,770
[Tom] You were?

583
00:42:56,771 --> 00:42:58,855
No, somebody else was.
I was with her, yes.

584
00:43:00,938 --> 00:43:02,230
I'm on it.

585
00:43:02,813 --> 00:43:03,771
Okay.

586
00:43:07,188 --> 00:43:10,270
You know, when I heard you wrote novels,
I wasn't surprised

587
00:43:10,271 --> 00:43:11,812
'cause you were always creative.

588
00:43:11,813 --> 00:43:13,895
Can we not do this right now?

589
00:43:13,896 --> 00:43:15,479
What are you talking about?

590
00:43:15,480 --> 00:43:17,687
[Tom] Can we not talk about
my fucking novel?

591
00:43:17,688 --> 00:43:21,604
- What are you talking about?
- Jake is who I want you to focus on. Jake.

592
00:43:21,605 --> 00:43:23,937
Not us, not me. Jake.

593
00:43:23,938 --> 00:43:26,645
I checked on Barnett. Nowhere to be found.

594
00:43:26,646 --> 00:43:28,771
Not a word from him
in the last six months.

595
00:43:29,980 --> 00:43:32,062
Okay, so what? We're back to nothing?

596
00:43:32,063 --> 00:43:34,437
Just a tape, and then a body,
and then another tape?

597
00:43:34,438 --> 00:43:36,020
I remember how it went with Carter.

598
00:43:36,021 --> 00:43:39,020
He's irrelevant.
He's doing life in prison. Doesn't matter.

599
00:43:39,021 --> 00:43:40,355
Tell that to my boy.

600
00:43:42,563 --> 00:43:45,480
What if whoever took Jake
knows he's your grandson?

601
00:43:46,438 --> 00:43:49,520
A different last name.
There's no connection to the Spencer kid.

602
00:43:49,521 --> 00:43:52,104
Absolutely no connection whatsoever.

603
00:43:52,105 --> 00:43:55,688
Yeah, but someone could find out.
I mean, Carter could be directing them.

604
00:43:56,730 --> 00:43:58,438
No, that's… that's going too far.

605
00:43:59,980 --> 00:44:02,062
Okay, but you're gonna go
talk to him, right?

606
00:44:02,063 --> 00:44:05,187
He'd just steer us in another direction,
in the wrong direction.

607
00:44:05,188 --> 00:44:07,520
So go, outsmart him.
You've done it once before.

608
00:44:07,521 --> 00:44:09,604
I didn't outsmart anything.
I just got lucky.

609
00:44:09,605 --> 00:44:12,230
So go get lucky again. What's the problem?

610
00:44:13,021 --> 00:44:16,312
- What, are you afraid of him?
- That man destroyed my life, my family.

611
00:44:16,313 --> 00:44:19,729
- You're damn right I'm afraid of him.
- No. You can't blame that on him.

612
00:44:19,730 --> 00:44:21,021
That was you.

613
00:44:25,230 --> 00:44:26,230
[door slams]

614
00:44:27,563 --> 00:44:29,104
[scribbling]

615
00:44:29,105 --> 00:44:31,230
[lock clicks, door opens]

616
00:44:37,396 --> 00:44:38,479
[door closes]

617
00:44:38,480 --> 00:44:40,480
[foreboding music playing]

618
00:44:43,938 --> 00:44:47,355
[Pete on tape] <i>Your husband threatened you
when you started asking questions.</i>

619
00:44:49,521 --> 00:44:52,855
<i>Did he ever give off any hints
about what he was doing before that?</i>

620
00:44:56,730 --> 00:44:59,187
<i>Behaviors out of step with his routine?</i>

621
00:44:59,188 --> 00:45:01,938
<i>Places he'd go? Objects in the house?</i>

622
00:45:02,438 --> 00:45:04,812
<i>Even days he smelled different,
or his clothes were soiled</i>

623
00:45:04,813 --> 00:45:06,813
<i>in a way that couldn't be explained?</i>

624
00:45:08,146 --> 00:45:11,105
<i>I'm asking all this
because there's still another boy missing.</i>

625
00:45:11,605 --> 00:45:14,395
<i>Tony Smith. He might still be alive.</i>

626
00:45:14,396 --> 00:45:15,604
[door opens]

627
00:45:15,605 --> 00:45:17,813
[Pete] <i>Frank put him somewhere,
and he's not talking.</i>

628
00:45:18,396 --> 00:45:20,105
<i>Maybe you can help us find him.</i>

629
00:45:21,313 --> 00:45:26,646
[cell phone buzzing]

630
00:45:27,146 --> 00:45:29,187
<i>- I've told you everything I know.</i>
- Yeah.

631
00:45:29,188 --> 00:45:31,188
[tense music playing]

632
00:46:17,188 --> 00:46:19,354
- [Pete] I'm here to see Beck.
- [man] Need some ID.

633
00:46:19,355 --> 00:46:20,480
[Beck] Let him through!

634
00:46:24,230 --> 00:46:25,396
Neil Spencer.

635
00:46:29,146 --> 00:46:30,146
No cameras?

636
00:46:31,146 --> 00:46:32,938
No. Not in the park.

637
00:46:36,480 --> 00:46:39,688
Could you check his nails, please?
His fingernails.

638
00:46:40,688 --> 00:46:41,688
Thank you.

639
00:46:43,313 --> 00:46:44,687
Carter would…

640
00:46:44,688 --> 00:46:47,646
He'd always cut their fingernails
before he strangled them.

641
00:46:48,188 --> 00:46:50,312
He didn't want them scratching his face.

642
00:46:50,313 --> 00:46:51,605
[Beck] Jesus.

643
00:46:53,938 --> 00:46:55,937
[camera shutter clicking]

644
00:46:55,938 --> 00:46:57,938
[indistinct chatter over radio]

645
00:46:58,563 --> 00:46:59,855
[over radio] <i>Copy that. Stand by.</i>

646
00:47:00,396 --> 00:47:01,355
What?

647
00:47:02,855 --> 00:47:03,980
Um…

648
00:47:05,646 --> 00:47:08,604
The shirt, the tapes.
That was all pretty much out there.

649
00:47:08,605 --> 00:47:09,938
It was all public.

650
00:47:11,021 --> 00:47:13,520
But not the cutting of the fingernails.
That wasn't public.

651
00:47:13,521 --> 00:47:16,980
Your accomplice theory, then.
Somebody who helped him back in the day.

652
00:47:18,105 --> 00:47:21,313
Well, why wait all these years
to get back to work?

653
00:47:28,021 --> 00:47:29,313
[sobbing]

654
00:47:34,480 --> 00:47:36,480
[stirring music playing]

655
00:47:49,146 --> 00:47:51,146
[music building]

656
00:48:07,646 --> 00:48:09,605
[stirring music continues]

657
00:48:40,355 --> 00:48:41,980
[door buzzes]

658
00:49:08,771 --> 00:49:10,270
[music fades]

659
00:49:10,271 --> 00:49:12,646
[Carter] You're a good man, Henry. Thanks.

660
00:49:19,980 --> 00:49:21,104
[door clangs]

661
00:49:21,105 --> 00:49:22,980
- Frank.
- Hi, Pete.

662
00:49:25,688 --> 00:49:27,062
Looking good.

663
00:49:27,063 --> 00:49:29,354
Thank you, Pete. Thank you.

664
00:49:29,355 --> 00:49:32,229
You know, 20, 30 years in the cage.

665
00:49:32,230 --> 00:49:34,438
Well, that'll keep you lean.

666
00:49:35,146 --> 00:49:36,063
Yeah.

667
00:49:38,063 --> 00:49:39,271
You still on the wagon?

668
00:49:41,146 --> 00:49:42,230
Good.

669
00:49:43,271 --> 00:49:45,021
That's very good. Really.

670
00:49:46,771 --> 00:49:50,021
I'm proud of you. If that means anything.

671
00:49:50,938 --> 00:49:52,687
'Cause, you know, whatever it is…

672
00:49:52,688 --> 00:49:54,438
[inhales, exhales sharply]

673
00:49:54,938 --> 00:49:57,480
…you know, your vice,

674
00:49:58,730 --> 00:50:01,104
you can try to lock it away,

675
00:50:01,105 --> 00:50:03,312
you can try to burn it
to the fucking ground,

676
00:50:03,313 --> 00:50:05,187
but it can't be killed.

677
00:50:05,188 --> 00:50:07,770
I mean, you can't kill it. You can't.

678
00:50:07,771 --> 00:50:10,645
Because it's like this guide or something.

679
00:50:10,646 --> 00:50:11,563
Right?

680
00:50:12,063 --> 00:50:16,354
I mean, it kind of takes hold of you
and controls you,

681
00:50:16,355 --> 00:50:18,230
and it becomes really

682
00:50:19,355 --> 00:50:23,438
the only thing in the world that exists.

683
00:50:23,980 --> 00:50:25,396
Everything else is just…

684
00:50:28,271 --> 00:50:29,312
window dressing.

685
00:50:29,313 --> 00:50:30,896
Kind of sad, really.

686
00:50:31,396 --> 00:50:32,937
How's that, Frank?

687
00:50:32,938 --> 00:50:34,562
Well, it's sad for you, isn't it?

688
00:50:34,563 --> 00:50:39,520
When you can't do the very thing

689
00:50:39,521 --> 00:50:41,771
that you were meant to do.

690
00:50:43,688 --> 00:50:44,605
I don't know.

691
00:50:46,313 --> 00:50:48,105
Might be better to just end it all.

692
00:50:50,396 --> 00:50:52,813
You could try that. Nobody'd miss you.

693
00:50:53,896 --> 00:50:56,062
A fair point. That's a fair point.

694
00:50:56,063 --> 00:50:57,187
I mean, yeah.

695
00:50:57,188 --> 00:51:00,188
But… but, I mean, for you, really, I mean…

696
00:51:03,813 --> 00:51:06,021
mostly it was endings, really.

697
00:51:06,605 --> 00:51:07,563
You know?

698
00:51:08,230 --> 00:51:11,271
Right? I mean, marriage, career,

699
00:51:12,313 --> 00:51:13,855
fatherhood. That didn't…

700
00:51:15,021 --> 00:51:17,730
Yeah, it's kind of like one long

701
00:51:18,605 --> 00:51:22,105
dirge on the road to your grave, right?

702
00:51:24,563 --> 00:51:26,771
Well, I'm hoping for a resurrection.

703
00:51:27,896 --> 00:51:29,355
Yours is unexpected.

704
00:51:30,021 --> 00:51:31,980
- [Carter chuckles]
- [Pete] Friend of yours?

705
00:51:32,563 --> 00:51:33,771
Friends? No.

706
00:51:36,771 --> 00:51:38,980
Men like you and I
don't have friends, Pete.

707
00:51:40,355 --> 00:51:41,770
We're meant to be alone.

708
00:51:41,771 --> 00:51:42,938
What else is there?

709
00:51:45,396 --> 00:51:47,438
- It speaks.
- [Beck] The work.

710
00:51:48,188 --> 00:51:49,896
It's all that's left, what you've done.

711
00:51:50,813 --> 00:51:53,730
This copycat, whoever he is,
he's showing you up.

712
00:51:54,480 --> 00:51:57,521
And if he keeps getting lucky, killing,

713
00:51:58,188 --> 00:51:59,895
what happens to your myth?

714
00:51:59,896 --> 00:52:01,563
You'll be replaced.

715
00:52:05,021 --> 00:52:06,271
She's pretty eager.

716
00:52:07,480 --> 00:52:09,979
What do you think, Pete?
How do you think she'll fare?

717
00:52:09,980 --> 00:52:11,396
As well as you?

718
00:52:12,355 --> 00:52:14,563
You should have seen him. Oh boy.

719
00:52:16,230 --> 00:52:17,355
Back then,

720
00:52:18,688 --> 00:52:21,604
so vital, so much life to live.

721
00:52:21,605 --> 00:52:23,771
He… Now, you know…

722
00:52:25,771 --> 00:52:26,812
you're all alone,

723
00:52:26,813 --> 00:52:29,687
cooking up your little dinners
in the dark.

724
00:52:29,688 --> 00:52:31,063
You know? I don't know.

725
00:52:33,146 --> 00:52:34,230
What do you think?

726
00:52:35,688 --> 00:52:37,563
Did it all turn out the way you'd hoped?

727
00:52:38,521 --> 00:52:39,438
You're here.

728
00:52:40,021 --> 00:52:40,938
Yeah.

729
00:52:42,938 --> 00:52:44,604
You gonna take credit for that?

730
00:52:44,605 --> 00:52:46,729
- Yes, I am. And comfort.
- [Carter] Okay.

731
00:52:46,730 --> 00:52:47,771
Okay.

732
00:52:48,938 --> 00:52:50,271
The killing stopped.

733
00:52:50,938 --> 00:52:52,813
The killing has stopped. [chuckles]

734
00:52:55,480 --> 00:52:57,062
But they haven't, have they?

735
00:52:57,063 --> 00:52:59,438
You know who's doing this, don't you?

736
00:53:02,355 --> 00:53:05,354
I'll tell you what.
You bring me my family, I might remember.

737
00:53:05,355 --> 00:53:06,520
Your family?

738
00:53:06,521 --> 00:53:07,646
My family. Tell her.

739
00:53:08,438 --> 00:53:09,687
Go ahead. Tell her, Pete.

740
00:53:09,688 --> 00:53:12,479
Tell her about my fucking family,

741
00:53:12,480 --> 00:53:14,104
how they sold me out.

742
00:53:14,105 --> 00:53:16,020
[breathes heavily]

743
00:53:16,021 --> 00:53:17,021
I'll tell you what.

744
00:53:17,646 --> 00:53:20,146
Why don't you bring me my wife

745
00:53:20,855 --> 00:53:21,938
and my son?

746
00:53:23,438 --> 00:53:25,271
Just bring them to me for…

747
00:53:27,938 --> 00:53:30,146
five minutes.
Just leave me alone with them.

748
00:53:30,855 --> 00:53:33,479
Go ahead. Five minutes.
I'll tell you everything you wanna know.

749
00:53:33,480 --> 00:53:36,938
I'll whisper it
right in your really cute little ear.

750
00:53:37,938 --> 00:53:39,938
Five minutes alone. Me and them.

751
00:53:41,563 --> 00:53:44,188
Hmm, don't worry about clean-up.
Clean-up's easy.

752
00:53:45,605 --> 00:53:47,270
Just hose down the room.

753
00:53:47,271 --> 00:53:48,521
[Pete] Okay, we're done.

754
00:53:50,063 --> 00:53:52,271
[Carter] You don't wanna hear about
the sixth victim?

755
00:53:52,771 --> 00:53:53,854
- Come on!
- Tony Smith?

756
00:53:53,855 --> 00:53:56,812
Tony Smith was five.
Come on, keep up. Tell her.

757
00:53:56,813 --> 00:53:58,895
You know, this guy's
still out there chasing him.

758
00:53:58,896 --> 00:54:01,354
He's on the ball.
He's out there chasing him still.

759
00:54:01,355 --> 00:54:03,604
I'm not playing your games this time.

760
00:54:03,605 --> 00:54:05,645
Yeah, well, your son is.
Boy, he is all in.

761
00:54:05,646 --> 00:54:07,562
How about those books of his, huh?

762
00:54:07,563 --> 00:54:11,229
The detective character.
Boy, he is trying to be you.

763
00:54:11,230 --> 00:54:14,730
Oh, he wants to be daddy.
But, you know, that's how it goes.

764
00:54:15,355 --> 00:54:18,021
'Cause when you're denied
your father's love,

765
00:54:19,396 --> 00:54:21,313
of course you mythologize him.

766
00:54:22,646 --> 00:54:25,355
She'll find out who we're talking about.

767
00:54:26,855 --> 00:54:28,438
Who you've become.

768
00:54:29,771 --> 00:54:31,437
[door buzzes]

769
00:54:31,438 --> 00:54:34,771
What did he mean back there?
His sixth victim?

770
00:54:40,771 --> 00:54:42,313
I asked you a question.

771
00:54:47,230 --> 00:54:51,813
First week Tony Smith was missing,
a thousand cops were searching for him.

772
00:54:52,855 --> 00:54:54,937
A month later, a hundred.

773
00:54:54,938 --> 00:54:57,355
A year after that, a dozen.

774
00:54:58,688 --> 00:55:01,230
Now there's only one.

775
00:55:02,563 --> 00:55:03,438
Me.

776
00:55:06,480 --> 00:55:08,395
[tape crackling]

777
00:55:08,396 --> 00:55:12,396
[whispering] Is there anything else
you want to say to your daddy?

778
00:55:23,396 --> 00:55:25,396
[foreboding music playing]

779
00:55:34,771 --> 00:55:37,105
[Jake] Why didn't you believe me?

780
00:55:39,188 --> 00:55:41,562
[man] Visitor rolls
for East Jersey State Prison.

781
00:55:41,563 --> 00:55:42,770
Checking for repeats.

782
00:55:42,771 --> 00:55:45,604
Cross-referencing criminal records,
connections to Carter.

783
00:55:45,605 --> 00:55:48,229
Good. I want every match released
in the last five years,

784
00:55:48,230 --> 00:55:51,104
and someone needs to reach out
to the FBI's field office in Phoenix.

785
00:55:51,105 --> 00:55:52,854
I'm sorry, what's in Phoenix?

786
00:55:52,855 --> 00:55:55,729
Carter's wife and kid are in
the witness protection program there.

787
00:55:55,730 --> 00:55:58,520
So if Carter is having someone else
do his killings for him,

788
00:55:58,521 --> 00:56:00,521
we need to let them know
as soon as possible.

789
00:56:15,521 --> 00:56:17,062
- You find something?
- [Pete] Maybe.

790
00:56:17,063 --> 00:56:19,937
Norman Collins visited Rahway last March,

791
00:56:19,938 --> 00:56:22,480
a few times last year.

792
00:56:29,021 --> 00:56:30,355
I think you should take him.

793
00:56:34,855 --> 00:56:39,645
Mr. Collins, Detective Amanda Beck.
Garretton PD. Can I come in?

794
00:56:39,646 --> 00:56:41,313
- Absolutely.
- [Beck] Okay.

795
00:56:43,438 --> 00:56:46,146
[lively operatic music playing
over stereo]

796
00:56:57,605 --> 00:57:00,479
[Beck] You recently went to see
an inmate at Rahway Prison.

797
00:57:00,480 --> 00:57:03,021
Victor Tyler, yes.

798
00:57:03,605 --> 00:57:04,979
May I ask why?

799
00:57:04,980 --> 00:57:07,854
[operatic music continues]

800
00:57:07,855 --> 00:57:09,313
He's a fascinating man.

801
00:57:10,396 --> 00:57:13,938
Life for kidnapping and murder.
You find that fascinating?

802
00:57:16,521 --> 00:57:20,271
This was worn by
a fairly notorious murderer in the 1960s.

803
00:57:20,771 --> 00:57:24,605
It cost me a small fortune,
but it's such a handsome piece.

804
00:57:25,396 --> 00:57:27,687
And the provenance is inviolable.

805
00:57:27,688 --> 00:57:30,480
[music continues playing over speakers]

806
00:57:32,563 --> 00:57:34,605
All completely above board.

807
00:57:39,313 --> 00:57:40,520
[music stops]

808
00:57:40,521 --> 00:57:42,938
I'm very well respected in my field.

809
00:57:44,063 --> 00:57:45,687
What field is that?

810
00:57:45,688 --> 00:57:47,980
I'm a collector, like you.

811
00:57:48,980 --> 00:57:52,562
You have your perps,
your cases, your obsessions.

812
00:57:52,563 --> 00:57:58,270
When ugly things happen to nice people,
you want to know why and where and who.

813
00:57:58,271 --> 00:58:04,063
For me, the interest is more
in the "how" and the "what."

814
00:58:04,896 --> 00:58:05,813
No, thanks.

815
00:58:06,896 --> 00:58:09,813
Come on. We're humoring each other.

816
00:58:16,688 --> 00:58:17,855
Can you feel that?

817
00:58:18,896 --> 00:58:19,813
What?

818
00:58:21,896 --> 00:58:23,480
What it must have been like

819
00:58:23,980 --> 00:58:27,979
stabbing your husband 46 times
in front of your best friends

820
00:58:27,980 --> 00:58:29,938
over a lost hand of bridge.

821
00:58:30,438 --> 00:58:31,271
[Beck scoffs]

822
00:58:32,230 --> 00:58:33,396
[screwdriver clatters]

823
00:58:34,396 --> 00:58:36,396
Where were you the night of April 10th?

824
00:58:38,980 --> 00:58:41,062
- Traveling.
- To?

825
00:58:41,063 --> 00:58:42,980
[Collins] Boston for an exhibition.

826
00:58:43,480 --> 00:58:45,688
[Beck] Do you have anything
to substantiate that?

827
00:58:53,980 --> 00:58:57,229
I didn't have anything to do with
those children being taken, Detective,

828
00:58:57,230 --> 00:58:58,813
if that's what you're here about.

829
00:59:14,230 --> 00:59:16,063
Well, well, well.

830
00:59:16,896 --> 00:59:18,604
What the fuck you want?

831
00:59:18,605 --> 00:59:22,354
Mr. Tyler, a man named Norman Collins
visited you about six months ago,

832
00:59:22,355 --> 00:59:23,812
twice in one week.

833
00:59:23,813 --> 00:59:26,063
I got no say who comes to see me.

834
00:59:28,313 --> 00:59:29,563
Obviously.

835
00:59:31,730 --> 00:59:34,979
You raped
and you murdered a 12-year-old girl.

836
00:59:34,980 --> 00:59:36,312
[Tyler] Hmm.

837
00:59:36,313 --> 00:59:39,312
I think you got a pretty good situation
here for doing something like that.

838
00:59:39,313 --> 00:59:40,729
Yeah.

839
00:59:40,730 --> 00:59:42,604
It's my winning personality.

840
00:59:42,605 --> 00:59:46,521
Did you ever pass anything
between Norman Collins and Frank Carter?

841
00:59:47,605 --> 00:59:48,938
Who's Frank Carter?

842
00:59:50,855 --> 00:59:53,105
[laughing]

843
00:59:56,355 --> 00:59:58,105
Maybe this will jog your memory.

844
01:00:00,396 --> 01:00:01,230
Hmm.

845
01:00:06,021 --> 01:00:07,020
Hmm?

846
01:00:07,021 --> 01:00:10,937
Why don't you two little piggies
take your bullshit deal

847
01:00:10,938 --> 01:00:13,562
and cry wee-wee-wee-wee all the way home?

848
01:00:13,563 --> 01:00:15,229
It's not a deal.

849
01:00:15,230 --> 01:00:17,855
It's an interstate
prisoner transfer order.

850
01:00:18,646 --> 01:00:22,395
[Pete] I don't know what life's gonna
be like for you in Lewisburg, Mr. Tyler,

851
01:00:22,396 --> 01:00:26,395
but I don't think it's gonna be very good
for a child rapist.

852
01:00:26,396 --> 01:00:29,105
But you're gonna need someone
like Frank Carter to protect you.

853
01:00:29,605 --> 01:00:31,729
Otherwise,
you're gonna have a big problem.

854
01:00:31,730 --> 01:00:33,396
[Beck] You feel like talking now?

855
01:00:35,188 --> 01:00:37,813
[cell phone buzzing]

856
01:00:38,396 --> 01:00:39,645
Dyson, talk to me.

857
01:00:39,646 --> 01:00:40,770
[Dyson] Another package.

858
01:00:40,771 --> 01:00:43,562
The address was recognized
before it was pulled from a box.

859
01:00:43,563 --> 01:00:45,105
I don't want anybody knowing about this.

860
01:00:46,355 --> 01:00:47,437
Already on it.

861
01:00:47,438 --> 01:00:49,438
Jake's tape just dropped.

862
01:00:58,313 --> 01:01:00,313
[tense pulsing music playing]

863
01:01:02,146 --> 01:01:05,438
[Beck] We have confirmation Carter's
been talking to someone on the outside.

864
01:01:05,938 --> 01:01:07,020
What?

865
01:01:07,021 --> 01:01:08,271
I'm so sorry.

866
01:01:09,105 --> 01:01:11,105
[tense pulsing music building]

867
01:01:18,438 --> 01:01:21,895
[through headphones] <i>♪ I love you
So what am I so afraid of? ♪</i>

868
01:01:21,896 --> 01:01:24,354
<i>♪ I'm afraid that I'm not sure of ♪</i>

869
01:01:24,355 --> 01:01:26,062
<i>♪ A love there is no cure… ♪</i>

870
01:01:26,063 --> 01:01:28,687
No. Jake was made to say those things.

871
01:01:28,688 --> 01:01:30,688
[sobbing quietly]

872
01:01:32,771 --> 01:01:35,187
He's alive.
That's the most important thing.

873
01:01:35,188 --> 01:01:36,271
Yeah, but…

874
01:01:38,563 --> 01:01:39,813
for how long?

875
01:01:41,146 --> 01:01:43,230
[Pete] Come on.
Let me take you home. Come on.

876
01:01:44,396 --> 01:01:45,271
Hmm?

877
01:01:47,980 --> 01:01:49,313
[sniffles] Okay.

878
01:01:55,605 --> 01:01:57,479
[microwave beeps]

879
01:01:57,480 --> 01:01:58,770
[door opens]

880
01:01:58,771 --> 01:02:00,063
[Tom] What's with that crack?

881
01:02:02,105 --> 01:02:06,354
Keeps opening up, no matter how many times
I try to plaster the damn thing.

882
01:02:06,355 --> 01:02:07,271
[Tom] Uh-huh.

883
01:02:18,438 --> 01:02:19,855
Thank you. Um…

884
01:02:23,313 --> 01:02:26,937
- Tom, we spoke to Frank Carter.
- You did?

885
01:02:26,938 --> 01:02:30,520
[Pete] He's had contact with someone
on the outside through another inmate.

886
01:02:30,521 --> 01:02:32,937
Someone named Victor Tyler.
He's a pedophile.

887
01:02:32,938 --> 01:02:35,979
And there was a burner phone found
in Tyler's cell.

888
01:02:35,980 --> 01:02:37,395
Forensics is on that now.

889
01:02:37,396 --> 01:02:38,396
Pedophile?

890
01:02:40,813 --> 01:02:43,271
Jesus fucking Christ.

891
01:02:47,230 --> 01:02:48,188
What are you doing?

892
01:02:49,855 --> 01:02:51,188
That's not gonna help.

893
01:02:52,396 --> 01:02:53,980
There's no booze in this house.

894
01:02:57,355 --> 01:02:58,438
Okay.

895
01:03:03,188 --> 01:03:04,645
I know. I know. I know.

896
01:03:04,646 --> 01:03:06,812
It's unbearable, I know.

897
01:03:06,813 --> 01:03:10,479
Jake's gonna come home,
but it has to be to a safe home.

898
01:03:10,480 --> 01:03:13,188
And his dad has to be all right.

899
01:03:13,855 --> 01:03:15,480
[Tom] I was drinking the night…

900
01:03:16,521 --> 01:03:17,520
We had an argument.

901
01:03:17,521 --> 01:03:20,271
"We had an argument."
I fucking yelled at him.

902
01:03:20,980 --> 01:03:26,895
To walk out that door into the dark,
he had to feel so alone.

903
01:03:26,896 --> 01:03:28,938
[somber music playing]

904
01:03:30,188 --> 01:03:33,687
When Rebecca died,
he found her at the bottom of the stairs,

905
01:03:33,688 --> 01:03:36,396
and now he can't even
climb a fucking flight of stairs.

906
01:03:38,480 --> 01:03:41,521
I mean, I thought it would be
a good change moving here.

907
01:03:42,605 --> 01:03:44,271
He held on to his mom's stuff.

908
01:03:46,563 --> 01:03:49,938
Photos and notes and old diaries and…

909
01:03:51,896 --> 01:03:53,687
In this satchel.

910
01:03:53,688 --> 01:03:56,855
He called it his Packet of Special Things.

911
01:03:59,063 --> 01:04:00,646
Hey, when you left us,

912
01:04:01,855 --> 01:04:03,854
didn't you want to reach out?

913
01:04:03,855 --> 01:04:06,229
Of course I… I… I… [sighs]

914
01:04:06,230 --> 01:04:07,230
Every day.

915
01:04:07,980 --> 01:04:10,688
Why didn't you? Weren't you curious?

916
01:04:14,188 --> 01:04:17,687
You know, she never spoke badly
about you, not once, Mom.

917
01:04:17,688 --> 01:04:19,271
Even after everything.

918
01:04:24,146 --> 01:04:27,229
There were times before you guys
moved away where your mother would say,

919
01:04:27,230 --> 01:04:30,938
"Look, you can see him,
but you can't be drinking."

920
01:04:31,771 --> 01:04:35,062
And so I would see you,
and I'd read you stories

921
01:04:35,063 --> 01:04:37,104
when you were about to go to sleep.

922
01:04:37,105 --> 01:04:40,438
And I would tell you how much I love you,
kiss you on the forehead.

923
01:04:41,730 --> 01:04:43,105
And she gave me that.

924
01:04:48,313 --> 01:04:49,646
Mr. Night?

925
01:04:51,146 --> 01:04:52,480
You're Mr. Night?

926
01:04:56,021 --> 01:04:56,980
You?

927
01:04:57,938 --> 01:04:59,355
That was you?

928
01:05:09,396 --> 01:05:11,396
[Pete] There's an extra bed
if you wanna stay.

929
01:05:12,688 --> 01:05:13,730
It's all made up.

930
01:05:18,355 --> 01:05:19,312
[rattling]

931
01:05:19,313 --> 01:05:23,771
[dog barking]

932
01:06:00,271 --> 01:06:02,271
[ominous music playing]

933
01:06:49,271 --> 01:06:51,020
They were pen pals.

934
01:06:51,021 --> 01:06:52,438
Did you know about this?

935
01:06:53,688 --> 01:06:56,937
What the fuck else is my dad not sharing?

936
01:06:56,938 --> 01:06:58,480
This isn't the place.

937
01:06:59,063 --> 01:06:59,938
What?

938
01:07:02,646 --> 01:07:05,520
Oh, is… is God listening to us right now?

939
01:07:05,521 --> 01:07:06,937
[cell phone buzzing]

940
01:07:06,938 --> 01:07:09,396
Maybe that's him, with some leads.

941
01:07:12,230 --> 01:07:14,271
[Beck] Tell me we have a search warrant.

942
01:07:16,188 --> 01:07:17,896
[Beck talking quietly on phone]

943
01:07:25,271 --> 01:07:28,188
[Beck continues talking quietly]

944
01:08:19,271 --> 01:08:21,438
Where the fuck is this guy going?

945
01:08:48,438 --> 01:08:50,562
Anything else you're not telling us?

946
01:08:50,563 --> 01:08:55,687
Carter sent those letters to hurt my son,
but I kept them secret to deny him that.

947
01:08:55,688 --> 01:08:58,855
You still kept them.
Norman Collins would be impressed.

948
01:09:03,771 --> 01:09:05,730
Fucking prick.

949
01:09:08,063 --> 01:09:09,187
You…

950
01:09:09,188 --> 01:09:10,646
[tires squeal]

951
01:09:11,438 --> 01:09:14,438
- [dramatic music playing]
- [kids clamoring]

952
01:09:16,313 --> 01:09:18,604
- [Tom] Where is he?
- [Collins] What are you doing? My God!

953
01:09:18,605 --> 01:09:20,187
Motherfucker! Where is he?

954
01:09:20,188 --> 01:09:21,520
Where's my boy?

955
01:09:21,521 --> 01:09:22,895
Oh God!

956
01:09:22,896 --> 01:09:25,395
- [Tom grunts]
- [Collins whimpers]

957
01:09:25,396 --> 01:09:27,145
Help! Help!

958
01:09:27,146 --> 01:09:28,312
- Where is he?
- Help!

959
01:09:28,313 --> 01:09:30,605
- [man] Hey! Come on!
- No!

960
01:09:31,271 --> 01:09:34,270
That guy kidnapped my son!
You're letting him get away!

961
01:09:34,271 --> 01:09:37,729
That's the Whisper Man!

962
01:09:37,730 --> 01:09:39,854
Back inside! Let's go! Now!

963
01:09:39,855 --> 01:09:41,146
[all clamoring]

964
01:09:41,730 --> 01:09:42,729
[teacher] Back inside!

965
01:09:42,730 --> 01:09:43,979
That's the Whisper Man!

966
01:09:43,980 --> 01:09:47,313
[Beck] What were you doing
in the basement of 13 Garholt Street?

967
01:09:48,063 --> 01:09:50,520
Uh, I don't know that address.

968
01:09:50,521 --> 01:09:52,645
- [Dyson] Norman, stop bullshitting us.
- [Beck scoffs]

969
01:09:52,646 --> 01:09:54,188
[Dyson] The owner saw you.

970
01:09:55,646 --> 01:09:57,729
If you're referring
to the man who just attacked me,

971
01:09:57,730 --> 01:09:59,312
I've never seen him before in my life.

972
01:09:59,313 --> 01:10:03,021
[Beck] My guys just searched your place.
This is underlined. So are the others.

973
01:10:05,396 --> 01:10:06,854
[Collins] I like his stories.

974
01:10:06,855 --> 01:10:08,438
[Dyson] What do you like about them?

975
01:10:08,980 --> 01:10:12,229
Well, he's got this dark mind,

976
01:10:12,230 --> 01:10:13,771
sort of like his daddy's.

977
01:10:14,271 --> 01:10:16,395
[Beck] We talked to Victor Tyler.

978
01:10:16,396 --> 01:10:20,354
We know that you used him
to pass on a private note to Frank Carter

979
01:10:20,355 --> 01:10:23,645
and a burner phone so he could communicate
with someone on the outside.

980
01:10:23,646 --> 01:10:27,771
And now children are disappearing
and turning up dead.

981
01:10:28,271 --> 01:10:30,145
I don't know, but it all points to you.

982
01:10:30,146 --> 01:10:33,021
- No. No, no, no, no, no.
- [Beck] Then what?

983
01:10:34,105 --> 01:10:36,021
Were you just getting his autograph?

984
01:10:36,813 --> 01:10:39,396
Another souvenir
for your sicko collection?

985
01:10:42,771 --> 01:10:44,730
I wouldn't hurt those kids, any kids.

986
01:10:46,563 --> 01:10:49,395
- Where the fuck is he going?
- [Pete] There's not enough to hold him.

987
01:10:49,396 --> 01:10:51,979
[Beck] He's accounted for both nights
the boys were kidnapped.

988
01:10:51,980 --> 01:10:54,395
In Jake's case,
that man was in another state.

989
01:10:54,396 --> 01:10:56,937
- So he couldn't have taken them.
- Not by himself.

990
01:10:56,938 --> 01:10:59,770
Collins wanted to press assault charges.
Still might.

991
01:10:59,771 --> 01:11:01,270
I hurt him? Are you kidding?

992
01:11:01,271 --> 01:11:03,437
Garretton PD will
only let you walk out of here tonight

993
01:11:03,438 --> 01:11:06,687
if you go home with your father here
and promise not to do anything stupid.

994
01:11:06,688 --> 01:11:07,855
[Tom] This man

995
01:11:08,480 --> 01:11:10,855
knows who has my boy.

996
01:11:18,021 --> 01:11:20,146
Please don't leave me.

997
01:11:27,980 --> 01:11:30,021
I was just trying to protect you.

998
01:11:33,105 --> 01:11:34,480
Yeah, well…

999
01:11:36,646 --> 01:11:41,438
Maybe that's the original sin
of… fathers everywhere.

1000
01:11:44,813 --> 01:11:45,855
We can't.

1001
01:11:55,980 --> 01:11:58,021
I'll be right back. [sighs]

1002
01:12:06,605 --> 01:12:07,688
[sighs]

1003
01:12:21,855 --> 01:12:24,105
[liquid pouring]

1004
01:12:32,688 --> 01:12:34,271
[dogs barking]

1005
01:12:42,355 --> 01:12:45,980
What was Norman doing in the basement?

1006
01:12:51,980 --> 01:12:54,771
If it really wasn't for Jake,
what was he looking for?

1007
01:13:39,355 --> 01:13:40,313
Dad.

1008
01:14:09,896 --> 01:14:12,896
[mysterious music playing]

1009
01:14:20,938 --> 01:14:22,938
[music building]

1010
01:14:43,313 --> 01:14:44,730
Boy in the floor.

1011
01:14:52,271 --> 01:14:54,562
[line ringing]

1012
01:14:54,563 --> 01:14:55,479
<i>Beck here.</i>

1013
01:14:55,480 --> 01:14:58,980
Yeah, we're at Garholt Street.
We just found Tony Smith.

1014
01:15:17,980 --> 01:15:19,271
Thirty years.

1015
01:15:20,646 --> 01:15:21,645
Collins knew.

1016
01:15:21,646 --> 01:15:23,980
What are we doing sitting here?

1017
01:15:34,230 --> 01:15:36,437
Hey, we got another body over here.

1018
01:15:36,438 --> 01:15:38,438
[dramatic music playing]

1019
01:15:48,146 --> 01:15:50,563
Some kind of blunt instrument.

1020
01:15:55,105 --> 01:15:56,229
[music fades]

1021
01:15:56,230 --> 01:15:59,270
["The Mikado: Behold
The Lord High Executioner" playing inside]

1022
01:15:59,271 --> 01:16:02,062
You better have
a very good excuse for harassing…

1023
01:16:02,063 --> 01:16:03,145
Hey! Hey!

1024
01:16:03,146 --> 01:16:06,145
We found Tony Smith's remains
on the Garholt property this morning.

1025
01:16:06,146 --> 01:16:07,396
[Pete] And another body.

1026
01:16:08,563 --> 01:16:09,604
[Beck] Provenance.

1027
01:16:09,605 --> 01:16:12,688
That's what you collectors call
where a thing comes from, right?

1028
01:16:13,896 --> 01:16:15,520
What's the provenance behind this?

1029
01:16:15,521 --> 01:16:18,354
Um, that was, uh, acquired off-market.

1030
01:16:18,355 --> 01:16:20,230
All aboveboard though, right?

1031
01:16:22,813 --> 01:16:24,812
Dominic Barnett. That name ring a bell?

1032
01:16:24,813 --> 01:16:27,187
He was found stuffed
in the wall of the basement.

1033
01:16:27,188 --> 01:16:29,021
His skull bashed in.

1034
01:16:31,230 --> 01:16:33,520
I don't know.
DNA will tell us if it's a match.

1035
01:16:33,521 --> 01:16:36,730
["Behold The Lord High Executioner"
continues playing over speakers]

1036
01:16:38,188 --> 01:16:39,979
Um, I want a lawyer.

1037
01:16:39,980 --> 01:16:42,396
You wanted in this game? You're in it.

1038
01:16:43,396 --> 01:16:45,479
I didn't hurt any children.

1039
01:16:45,480 --> 01:16:49,562
[sirens wailing]

1040
01:16:49,563 --> 01:16:50,895
Okay.

1041
01:16:50,896 --> 01:16:54,062
I paid Frank Carter for access.

1042
01:16:54,063 --> 01:16:57,354
Access? Access to who? Tony Smith?

1043
01:16:57,355 --> 01:16:59,979
- Maybe grab something for your collection?
- Okay. Yes.

1044
01:16:59,980 --> 01:17:01,812
So he pointed you to Dominic Barnett?

1045
01:17:01,813 --> 01:17:05,104
Yeah. Um, they… they were friends
back in the day.

1046
01:17:05,105 --> 01:17:07,312
Friends? They weren't friends.
They were accomplices.

1047
01:17:07,313 --> 01:17:09,937
What happened between you and Dominic
when you got to the house?

1048
01:17:09,938 --> 01:17:11,979
- He, um…
- [Pete] What happened?

1049
01:17:11,980 --> 01:17:14,687
He said, uh… He…

1050
01:17:14,688 --> 01:17:16,020
[breathing unsteadily]

1051
01:17:16,021 --> 01:17:17,021
[Pete] What happened?

1052
01:17:17,730 --> 01:17:21,437
In the basement,
he made me feel very small,

1053
01:17:21,438 --> 01:17:25,187
saying that I was a tourist
and that I was a Peeping Tom.

1054
01:17:25,188 --> 01:17:27,354
That I could jerk off but never fuck.

1055
01:17:27,355 --> 01:17:28,395
So you killed him?

1056
01:17:28,396 --> 01:17:31,604
[Pete] You killed him, didn't you?
And that I don't care about.

1057
01:17:31,605 --> 01:17:34,063
All I care about is
finding Jake Kennedy alive.

1058
01:17:34,938 --> 01:17:36,312
Do you understand?

1059
01:17:36,313 --> 01:17:37,770
[panting]

1060
01:17:37,771 --> 01:17:38,771
I can't…

1061
01:17:39,271 --> 01:17:40,980
- I can't go to prison.
- [Pete] You can't?

1062
01:17:41,563 --> 01:17:44,063
Well, that's too bad.
You're going to prison.

1063
01:17:44,646 --> 01:17:46,062
For a long time.

1064
01:17:46,063 --> 01:17:48,646
So you tell us everything
we need to know right now.

1065
01:17:49,646 --> 01:17:53,437
You just said you paid Frank Carter
for access to his last victim, Tony Smith,

1066
01:17:53,438 --> 01:17:55,937
who was never found.
Is that a fair statement?

1067
01:17:55,938 --> 01:17:57,854
- Yes.
- [Beck] Paid with what?

1068
01:17:57,855 --> 01:18:00,855
Carter's in prison for life.
No use for money.

1069
01:18:01,355 --> 01:18:03,896
No family anymore. What did you trade?

1070
01:18:05,938 --> 01:18:07,770
I connected him with someone.

1071
01:18:07,771 --> 01:18:10,563
Who? Norman, who did you connect him to?

1072
01:18:11,146 --> 01:18:12,230
[Beck] Who, Norman?

1073
01:18:14,438 --> 01:18:17,605
I was the only one who ever saw it.
In the eyes.

1074
01:18:18,105 --> 01:18:20,312
The eyes? Who are you talking about?

1075
01:18:20,313 --> 01:18:23,812
[whispers] I just thought that, you know,
they'd wanna get to know each other.

1076
01:18:23,813 --> 01:18:27,270
I never thought that…
that it was gonna start again.

1077
01:18:27,271 --> 01:18:30,438
Norman, we need a name. Who is it?

1078
01:18:31,521 --> 01:18:32,937
[Beck] The eyes.

1079
01:18:32,938 --> 01:18:34,938
The eyes. Who are you talking about?

1080
01:18:41,896 --> 01:18:43,480
[Beck screams, pants]

1081
01:18:44,021 --> 01:18:45,271
[Beck yelps]

1082
01:18:46,480 --> 01:18:47,395
We need a bus!

1083
01:18:47,396 --> 01:18:50,729
- Help! We need an ambulance!
- Where's Jake? Tell me, where's Jake?

1084
01:18:50,730 --> 01:18:53,354
That's the one thing you can do.
Tell me, where's Jake, please?

1085
01:18:53,355 --> 01:18:55,645
Where is Jake? Where's Jake?

1086
01:18:55,646 --> 01:18:58,020
- [man] Sir!
- [Pete] Just tell me where he is, please.

1087
01:18:58,021 --> 01:18:59,188
[officer] Please stand back!

1088
01:18:59,896 --> 01:19:01,229
Come on.

1089
01:19:01,230 --> 01:19:02,437
Stay with me.

1090
01:19:02,438 --> 01:19:05,938
[ominous music playing]

1091
01:19:28,521 --> 01:19:29,812
[music fades]

1092
01:19:29,813 --> 01:19:33,437
Tom was right. We should have beat
whatever the hell we needed out of him.

1093
01:19:33,438 --> 01:19:35,895
Norman said that he thought
Frank Carter would be interested

1094
01:19:35,896 --> 01:19:37,937
in getting to know this person. Why?

1095
01:19:37,938 --> 01:19:41,187
Why invest in someone
he'll never know, never meet?

1096
01:19:41,188 --> 01:19:42,313
Makes no sense.

1097
01:19:43,063 --> 01:19:45,646
Who is more important to Frank Carter
than you?

1098
01:19:49,313 --> 01:19:51,313
[indistinct background chatter]

1099
01:19:54,188 --> 01:19:57,480
What did Carter say to us
when we were leaving?

1100
01:19:57,980 --> 01:19:59,396
[Beck] The sixth victim?

1101
01:20:00,355 --> 01:20:01,230
[Pete] No.

1102
01:20:02,771 --> 01:20:04,730
About my son's novels.

1103
01:20:06,605 --> 01:20:08,146
He's trying to be you.

1104
01:20:12,396 --> 01:20:14,605
Pull up the interview
with Frank Carter's wife.

1105
01:20:19,146 --> 01:20:21,188
That's the one. Play it.

1106
01:20:22,896 --> 01:20:24,688
<i>I was afraid for my son.</i>

1107
01:20:25,896 --> 01:20:28,770
[Pete on video] <i>You don't have
to be afraid anymore, Mrs. Carter.</i>

1108
01:20:28,771 --> 01:20:29,980
<i>You're safe now.</i>

1109
01:20:31,146 --> 01:20:34,938
<i>There's another boy still missing, though,
and he might still be alive.</i>

1110
01:20:35,438 --> 01:20:37,104
<i>You can help us find him.</i>

1111
01:20:37,105 --> 01:20:38,771
<i>He's somebody's son too.</i>

1112
01:20:39,605 --> 01:20:41,355
<i>I've told you everything I know.</i>

1113
01:20:52,938 --> 01:20:55,895
[Beck] "When we're denied
our father's love,

1114
01:20:55,896 --> 01:20:57,480
we mythologize him."

1115
01:20:59,313 --> 01:21:00,271
It's him.

1116
01:21:06,146 --> 01:21:08,980
Do you ever feel like a boy in the floor,

1117
01:21:10,605 --> 01:21:12,605
underneath everyone's feet,

1118
01:21:13,563 --> 01:21:15,355
who no one knows is there?

1119
01:21:16,563 --> 01:21:17,605
I do.

1120
01:21:19,188 --> 01:21:22,855
Did the boy in the floor
go to sleep forever?

1121
01:21:26,146 --> 01:21:27,230
He did.

1122
01:21:32,896 --> 01:21:36,105
Are you going to make me
go to sleep forever?

1123
01:21:37,146 --> 01:21:39,146
I'm going to bring you home.

1124
01:21:45,230 --> 01:21:48,062
[Beck] <i>After Carter's conviction,
the family moved out west</i>

1125
01:21:48,063 --> 01:21:49,395
and assumed new identities.

1126
01:21:49,396 --> 01:21:52,187
We have no name, no ID.

1127
01:21:52,188 --> 01:21:55,979
We're negotiating with the FBI
to release whatever records they do have

1128
01:21:55,980 --> 01:21:59,187
because, technically, Francis Jr.
is still under their protection.

1129
01:21:59,188 --> 01:22:02,854
In the meantime, we need to canvas
anyone and everyone

1130
01:22:02,855 --> 01:22:05,020
in Hillcrest
and the surrounding neighborhoods.

1131
01:22:05,021 --> 01:22:08,104
If Francis Jr. is here,
someone knows where to find him.

1132
01:22:08,105 --> 01:22:09,230
Let's go.

1133
01:22:16,980 --> 01:22:19,020
[sirens wailing]

1134
01:22:19,021 --> 01:22:20,437
[over radio] <i>All units be advised.</i>

1135
01:22:20,438 --> 01:22:23,312
<i>The suspect has been identified
as Francis Carter, Jr.,</i>

1136
01:22:23,313 --> 01:22:25,145
<i>residing in Garretton.</i>

1137
01:22:25,146 --> 01:22:29,395
<i>We'll conduct a block-by-block canvas
in an attempt to locate the suspect.</i>

1138
01:22:29,396 --> 01:22:30,271
<i>Car 431.</i>

1139
01:22:30,980 --> 01:22:33,771
<i>Cover the 400 block of Lafayette,
heading east.</i>

1140
01:22:34,355 --> 01:22:38,855
<i>Car 595. Cover Maple Avenue
on the 200 block, heading south.</i>

1141
01:22:53,605 --> 01:22:55,105
[door buzzing]

1142
01:23:15,771 --> 01:23:17,396
[door locking]

1143
01:23:19,396 --> 01:23:21,188
How's your grandson, Pete?

1144
01:23:22,730 --> 01:23:25,604
Good afternoon.
Detective Amanda Beck, Garretton PD.

1145
01:23:25,605 --> 01:23:27,438
I'm looking for Richard Sharmatz.

1146
01:23:28,980 --> 01:23:34,229
Ah, Dr. Sharmatz, uh, passed away
about a year ago.

1147
01:23:34,230 --> 01:23:35,729
Oh, his name's still on the title.

1148
01:23:35,730 --> 01:23:38,104
His family rents the house to me.

1149
01:23:38,105 --> 01:23:40,312
He was a mentor of… of mine.

1150
01:23:40,313 --> 01:23:42,395
- [Beck] Oh.
- I'm George Carringdon.

1151
01:23:42,396 --> 01:23:43,312
- Hi.
- Hi.

1152
01:23:43,313 --> 01:23:45,271
You a child psychologist as well?

1153
01:23:45,771 --> 01:23:47,187
Teaching assistant.

1154
01:23:47,188 --> 01:23:48,105
Where?

1155
01:23:49,021 --> 01:23:50,188
- Rose Terrace.
- [Beck] Huh.

1156
01:23:50,855 --> 01:23:53,355
Do you know a Jake Kennedy?
He was a student there.

1157
01:23:54,980 --> 01:23:57,605
Not until they announced what happened.

1158
01:23:58,146 --> 01:24:01,812
I… I probably saw him
running through the halls out at recess,

1159
01:24:01,813 --> 01:24:04,729
but, um, I work with
the special needs kids.

1160
01:24:04,730 --> 01:24:06,938
- Oh.
- So I wouldn't have known him by name.

1161
01:24:08,105 --> 01:24:09,188
Do you want to come in?

1162
01:24:09,688 --> 01:24:10,730
[door closes]

1163
01:24:15,646 --> 01:24:18,145
Did you, by any chance,
know the Carter family back in the day?

1164
01:24:18,146 --> 01:24:20,770
Frank and Jane, their son Francis Jr.

1165
01:24:20,771 --> 01:24:21,730
Of them.

1166
01:24:22,230 --> 01:24:26,145
My parents tried to keep me away
from all that stuff. Didn't work.

1167
01:24:26,146 --> 01:24:28,395
We know you've been in communication
with your son,

1168
01:24:28,396 --> 01:24:29,771
prodding him with these killings.

1169
01:24:30,355 --> 01:24:33,812
Boy left home, and now he's back.

1170
01:24:33,813 --> 01:24:34,896
Got lost.

1171
01:24:36,063 --> 01:24:37,313
He's back home now.

1172
01:24:37,813 --> 01:24:39,020
That surprise you?

1173
01:24:39,021 --> 01:24:40,270
Not really, no.

1174
01:24:40,271 --> 01:24:44,021
I mean, Francis has always been weak.
Look how he…

1175
01:24:44,771 --> 01:24:46,688
how he fucked up the first try.

1176
01:24:48,146 --> 01:24:49,895
[Beck] I guess it's hard with kids.

1177
01:24:49,896 --> 01:24:52,188
Well, scary stories are like water.

1178
01:24:54,688 --> 01:24:57,020
They always find their way
through the cracks.

1179
01:24:57,021 --> 01:25:01,605
I remember growing up in Fair Lawn.
There was this rhyme.

1180
01:25:02,980 --> 01:25:04,854
<i>If you leave a door half open</i>

1181
01:25:04,855 --> 01:25:06,895
<i>Soon you'll hear the whisper spoken</i>

1182
01:25:06,896 --> 01:25:09,770
- [both] <i>If your window's…</i>
- [George] <i>…left unlatched</i>

1183
01:25:09,771 --> 01:25:11,646
<i>You'll hear him tapping at the glass</i>

1184
01:25:12,146 --> 01:25:14,563
<i>- If you're lonely…</i>
- [both] <i>…sad, or blue…</i>

1185
01:25:15,188 --> 01:25:16,562
[clock ticking]

1186
01:25:16,563 --> 01:25:18,605
<i>The Whisper Man will come for you</i>

1187
01:25:25,438 --> 01:25:27,771
Been a long time
since I've heard that one.

1188
01:25:29,146 --> 01:25:33,229
[kettle whistling]

1189
01:25:33,230 --> 01:25:35,188
I was making tea. You want a cup?

1190
01:25:40,563 --> 01:25:43,020
I get now
why you always covered their faces.

1191
01:25:43,021 --> 01:25:46,312
I thought it was 'cause you couldn't look
at 'em or didn't want them looking at you.

1192
01:25:46,313 --> 01:25:48,479
Nah, I could look at their faces
just fine.

1193
01:25:48,480 --> 01:25:49,979
[Pete] Oh, that's bullshit. Come on.

1194
01:25:49,980 --> 01:25:52,062
You know there was someone
you were imagining

1195
01:25:52,063 --> 01:25:55,146
you wanted to get a hold of
but you couldn't really get your hands on.

1196
01:25:56,896 --> 01:25:59,020
It was too painful, too messy,

1197
01:25:59,021 --> 01:26:00,354
too close to home.

1198
01:26:00,355 --> 01:26:03,521
Well… home is where the heart is, Pete.

1199
01:26:04,688 --> 01:26:09,105
[George] Is there some sort of connection
between Frank Carter and Dr. Sharmatz?

1200
01:26:10,105 --> 01:26:14,229
He counseled Carter's son,
according to records.

1201
01:26:14,230 --> 01:26:16,604
[ominous music playing]

1202
01:26:16,605 --> 01:26:18,938
[George] Police must be stretched
pretty thin.

1203
01:26:20,188 --> 01:26:22,063
No partner, I see.

1204
01:26:23,646 --> 01:26:25,813
Everybody has their ground to cover.

1205
01:26:26,480 --> 01:26:31,021
I know the parents will be relieved
that you're chasing down some leads.

1206
01:26:31,646 --> 01:26:34,271
Yeah. Kids, too, I'm guessing.

1207
01:26:34,771 --> 01:26:37,605
Francis is learning his own lessons
right now.

1208
01:26:38,105 --> 01:26:40,438
Yeah. Like you did with your father?

1209
01:26:41,980 --> 01:26:43,520
The way he taught you.

1210
01:26:43,521 --> 01:26:45,937
Whispering to you in bed
while he was fucking you up the ass?

1211
01:26:45,938 --> 01:26:47,562
[laughs] You better shut up.

1212
01:26:47,563 --> 01:26:49,645
How'd you handle those situations, Frank?

1213
01:26:49,646 --> 01:26:52,312
Did you wish you were somewhere
like the kids you took did too?

1214
01:26:52,313 --> 01:26:53,562
- Fuck you.
- [Pete] Ah.

1215
01:26:53,563 --> 01:26:55,812
Your father whet his appetite
with his own son.

1216
01:26:55,813 --> 01:26:58,271
- [Carter] Fuck you.
- But you, you were the weak one.

1217
01:27:01,980 --> 01:27:04,520
I actually respect you, Frank.
You know that?

1218
01:27:04,521 --> 01:27:08,396
You tried to stop yourself from doing
what you really wanted to do to your boy.

1219
01:27:08,896 --> 01:27:09,896
Yeah.

1220
01:27:11,063 --> 01:27:12,812
So you preyed on others.

1221
01:27:12,813 --> 01:27:15,687
When we catch your son,
and we're gonna catch him very soon…

1222
01:27:15,688 --> 01:27:18,312
- Yeah?
- You're never gonna hear from him again.

1223
01:27:18,313 --> 01:27:20,604
Oh, really? So…

1224
01:27:20,605 --> 01:27:22,605
So there's another possibility.

1225
01:27:23,771 --> 01:27:24,730
Jake.

1226
01:27:25,521 --> 01:27:27,062
You can tell me where he is.

1227
01:27:27,063 --> 01:27:27,896
[laughs softly]

1228
01:27:30,855 --> 01:27:32,729
Why would I do that before the deed?

1229
01:27:32,730 --> 01:27:35,605
Because the Whisper Man,
the real one, isn't done yet.

1230
01:27:36,188 --> 01:27:39,104
Because there's only one child
in this whole world

1231
01:27:39,105 --> 01:27:41,563
that he truly, really wants.

1232
01:27:42,063 --> 01:27:43,855
And I can deliver him to you.

1233
01:27:45,355 --> 01:27:46,605
[Carter] My son?

1234
01:27:51,355 --> 01:27:52,395
Here?

1235
01:27:52,396 --> 01:27:55,563
A father does what needs to be done.
Wouldn't you agree?

1236
01:27:59,938 --> 01:28:02,479
[Beck] If you think of anyone
that might know the Carter family,

1237
01:28:02,480 --> 01:28:06,188
especially Francis Jr.,
please have them call me, okay?

1238
01:28:09,688 --> 01:28:11,271
- Of course.
- [cell phone chimes]

1239
01:28:12,146 --> 01:28:14,146
[clock ticking]

1240
01:28:20,813 --> 01:28:22,687
- [George grunts]
- [Beck] Oh fuck!

1241
01:28:22,688 --> 01:28:25,020
[Beck panting]

1242
01:28:25,021 --> 01:28:27,605
[running footsteps]

1243
01:28:30,646 --> 01:28:34,645
This is Beck. I need backup.
59 Hellerman Street. I found our suspect.

1244
01:28:34,646 --> 01:28:36,480
- [man] <i>Copy that.</i>
- [thud]

1245
01:28:37,063 --> 01:28:38,396
Jake Kennedy?

1246
01:28:39,271 --> 01:28:40,687
This is the police.

1247
01:28:40,688 --> 01:28:42,688
[tense music playing]

1248
01:29:47,188 --> 01:29:49,188
[Beck panting]

1249
01:30:13,688 --> 01:30:15,563
[air hisses]

1250
01:30:26,438 --> 01:30:27,771
Scream.

1251
01:30:31,605 --> 01:30:34,395
[Jake yelling] Help!

1252
01:30:34,396 --> 01:30:36,396
[pulsing tense music building]

1253
01:30:42,730 --> 01:30:45,230
- [George grunts]
- [Beck screams]

1254
01:30:46,355 --> 01:30:47,520
[George grunts]

1255
01:30:47,521 --> 01:30:48,355
[Beck groans]

1256
01:30:55,396 --> 01:30:56,230
[door unlocks]

1257
01:30:57,063 --> 01:30:59,521
[yelling] Get up! Come on!

1258
01:31:12,021 --> 01:31:13,188
- [Beck grunts]
- [George yells]

1259
01:31:17,438 --> 01:31:19,730
[Jake whimpering]

1260
01:31:21,438 --> 01:31:23,270
[panting] Run!

1261
01:31:23,271 --> 01:31:25,895
[whimpering]

1262
01:31:25,896 --> 01:31:26,855
[Beck] Run!

1263
01:31:32,105 --> 01:31:33,438
[George groans]

1264
01:31:38,813 --> 01:31:40,229
Help!

1265
01:31:40,230 --> 01:31:41,271
Stop!

1266
01:31:42,313 --> 01:31:44,980
Help! Help!

1267
01:31:52,521 --> 01:31:53,895
[engine turns over]

1268
01:31:53,896 --> 01:31:55,355
[car pulls away]

1269
01:32:07,563 --> 01:32:11,229
[buzzing]

1270
01:32:11,230 --> 01:32:14,855
[sirens wailing]

1271
01:32:15,563 --> 01:32:17,437
<i>Detective Beck. Leave a message.</i>

1272
01:32:17,438 --> 01:32:19,938
Beck. Yeah. It's me.

1273
01:32:20,688 --> 01:32:23,270
I spoke to Carter.
They have a plan for Jake.

1274
01:32:23,271 --> 01:32:25,271
[unsettling music playing]

1275
01:32:34,730 --> 01:32:36,187
[tapping on phone]

1276
01:32:36,188 --> 01:32:37,771
[line ringing]

1277
01:32:39,146 --> 01:32:41,354
[operator] <i>Garretton Police.
What's your emergency?</i>

1278
01:32:41,355 --> 01:32:43,479
I just saw the missing boy, Jake Kennedy.

1279
01:32:43,480 --> 01:32:46,270
He was with a man,
Route 23, south of Sussex.

1280
01:32:46,271 --> 01:32:48,770
<i>Dispatch 10-17. We have units en route.</i>

1281
01:32:48,771 --> 01:32:51,438
<i>Can I please have your name
and a callback number?</i>

1282
01:32:59,438 --> 01:33:03,063
[siren wailing]

1283
01:33:16,855 --> 01:33:18,771
[Jake panting]

1284
01:33:20,188 --> 01:33:22,563
- [line ringing]
- What the hell?

1285
01:33:24,355 --> 01:33:27,312
[cell phone buzzing]

1286
01:33:27,313 --> 01:33:29,730
- [line continues ringing]
- Come on, Tom. Please pick up.

1287
01:33:39,105 --> 01:33:41,562
[line continues ringing]

1288
01:33:41,563 --> 01:33:42,520
[Tom] <i>Dad?</i>

1289
01:33:42,521 --> 01:33:44,521
[unsettling music continues playing]

1290
01:33:50,521 --> 01:33:51,688
[George] Sh.

1291
01:34:10,063 --> 01:34:12,063
[eerie music playing]

1292
01:34:24,313 --> 01:34:27,438
[alarm blaring]

1293
01:35:11,813 --> 01:35:13,604
- [Jake] I can't breathe!
- Jake!

1294
01:35:13,605 --> 01:35:14,729
[Jake] Dad, help!

1295
01:35:14,730 --> 01:35:18,062
[both grunt]

1296
01:35:18,063 --> 01:35:20,813
[Jake yelling]

1297
01:35:23,063 --> 01:35:25,063
[both grunting]

1298
01:35:27,313 --> 01:35:28,313
[Jake yells]

1299
01:35:30,188 --> 01:35:31,896
[Jake] Help!

1300
01:35:35,688 --> 01:35:36,521
[grunts]

1301
01:35:40,355 --> 01:35:42,938
- [Jake yelling]
- [Tom] Jake!

1302
01:35:44,313 --> 01:35:46,355
[Jake continues yelling]

1303
01:35:49,355 --> 01:35:50,771
[Jake panting]

1304
01:35:52,730 --> 01:35:54,355
Oh, Jake. It's okay.

1305
01:35:55,063 --> 01:35:56,146
[grunts]

1306
01:35:58,771 --> 01:36:00,521
Come on. Come on. Go.

1307
01:36:01,188 --> 01:36:03,896
[dramatic music playing]

1308
01:36:12,646 --> 01:36:14,188
- [Tom moans]
- Dad!

1309
01:36:19,605 --> 01:36:20,563
[Jake] Dad!

1310
01:36:21,396 --> 01:36:23,355
No!

1311
01:36:25,855 --> 01:36:29,438
Dad!

1312
01:36:30,063 --> 01:36:31,062
[Pete] Jake!

1313
01:36:31,063 --> 01:36:32,355
- [Jake] Dad!
- Jake!

1314
01:36:34,313 --> 01:36:36,396
Run! Run, Jake!

1315
01:36:36,896 --> 01:36:37,730
Run!

1316
01:36:39,896 --> 01:36:40,813
[groans]

1317
01:36:49,980 --> 01:36:52,354
Tommy, Tommy. Get Jake.

1318
01:36:52,355 --> 01:36:54,395
- Go get Jake.
- Dad! What?

1319
01:36:54,396 --> 01:36:56,271
- I love you.
- I love you.

1320
01:37:29,021 --> 01:37:30,355
[both grunt]

1321
01:37:43,605 --> 01:37:46,021
[both grunt]

1322
01:37:50,396 --> 01:37:51,938
Daddy!

1323
01:37:53,063 --> 01:37:54,605
Daddy!

1324
01:37:57,730 --> 01:37:58,812
[music calms]

1325
01:37:58,813 --> 01:38:01,855
[Jake panting]

1326
01:38:04,063 --> 01:38:05,105
[Tom] Jake.

1327
01:38:06,105 --> 01:38:09,230
Just stay. Stay there.

1328
01:38:10,355 --> 01:38:13,438
Jake, close your eyes.

1329
01:38:16,063 --> 01:38:17,355
[George] Agh!

1330
01:38:19,813 --> 01:38:21,105
[groaning]

1331
01:38:33,396 --> 01:38:36,396
[George breathing heavily]

1332
01:39:30,063 --> 01:39:32,688
[mysterious music playing]

1333
01:40:12,063 --> 01:40:16,145
[door unlocks, opens]

1334
01:40:16,146 --> 01:40:17,980
[man] Just make it quick, Carter.

1335
01:40:33,188 --> 01:40:34,771
Skin to skin,

1336
01:40:36,813 --> 01:40:38,771
like they said in the hospital,

1337
01:40:39,646 --> 01:40:41,770
to bond you to me.

1338
01:40:41,771 --> 01:40:43,771
[unsettling music playing]

1339
01:40:55,355 --> 01:40:56,896
[gasping]

1340
01:41:00,521 --> 01:41:02,604
[George choking]

1341
01:41:02,605 --> 01:41:04,605
[unsettling music building]

1342
01:41:27,646 --> 01:41:29,646
[music calms]

1343
01:41:46,063 --> 01:41:49,063
[solemn music playing]

1344
01:42:02,605 --> 01:42:04,605
[music fades]

1345
01:42:08,521 --> 01:42:11,145
What's Pearl Jam?

1346
01:42:11,146 --> 01:42:13,145
What? A band!

1347
01:42:13,146 --> 01:42:14,854
Clearly failed as a father.

1348
01:42:14,855 --> 01:42:16,980
It was our first concert, your mom and me.

1349
01:42:20,688 --> 01:42:21,688
She saved me.

1350
01:42:30,063 --> 01:42:31,063
Mommy?

1351
01:42:31,563 --> 01:42:32,480
Mm-hmm.

1352
01:42:35,188 --> 01:42:36,396
Yeah, me too.

1353
01:42:37,396 --> 01:42:39,396
[kids shouting outside]

1354
01:42:40,646 --> 01:42:42,313
Can I go play?

1355
01:42:44,021 --> 01:42:44,980
Yeah, dude.

1356
01:42:46,938 --> 01:42:48,104
Get out there.

1357
01:42:48,105 --> 01:42:49,688
- What are you doing in here?
- [chuckles]

1358
01:42:51,730 --> 01:42:52,813
[door opens]

1359
01:42:54,355 --> 01:42:55,480
[door closes]

1360
01:42:56,896 --> 01:42:58,145
[Jake] Hey, guys!

1361
01:42:58,146 --> 01:42:59,813
[kids continue shouting]

1362
01:43:29,730 --> 01:43:32,021
[gentle ethereal music playing]

1363
01:44:14,771 --> 01:44:17,021
[ethereal music continues]

1364
01:45:32,563 --> 01:45:34,063
[music fades]

1365
01:45:36,438 --> 01:45:38,438
[haunting music playing]

1366
01:49:03,438 --> 01:49:05,438
[somber music playing]

1367
01:51:01,021 --> 01:51:03,021
[music fades]

